1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:00,793
[Previously on "ALL or NOTHING"]
[EGYPT]

2
00:00:00,794 --> 00:00:02,300
The pyramid.

3
00:00:02,301 --> 00:00:03,732
The Sphinx.

4
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:04,633
The capital, Cairo.

5
00:00:04,634 --> 00:00:06,100
[ALL or NOTHING]
A mysterious country.

6
00:00:06,101 --> 00:00:07,192
I'm really in Egypt.

7
00:00:07,199 --> 00:00:09,406
[The six men arrive in the golden city]
It’s been one of my dreams.

8
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:10,700
What does this mean?
I didn't get it!

9
00:00:10,701 --> 00:00:12,007
[Goofball eldest brother, LEETEUK]
Why can’t I understand this?

10
00:00:12,008 --> 00:00:12,833
I didn't understand it.

11
00:00:12,834 --> 00:00:14,133
[Knock knock]
Something healthy means smaller portions.

12
00:00:14,134 --> 00:00:15,094
[Strategist SHINDONG]
This was all part of the plan.

13
00:00:15,095 --> 00:00:16,133
SHINDONG, you’re super strategic.

14
00:00:16,134 --> 00:00:17,133
[The gentle and soft type?!]

15
00:00:17,134 --> 00:00:18,498
[A man of unexpected charms, DAWN]
I should show you my unexpected side.

16
00:00:18,499 --> 00:00:19,467
Wow!

17
00:00:19,468 --> 00:00:20,567
I’m all about chasing romance.

18
00:00:20,568 --> 00:00:22,800
[Team Romance, JOHNNY]
In a way, it could be romantic, right?

19
00:00:22,801 --> 00:00:24,067
I'm gonna win, no matter what.

20
00:00:24,068 --> 00:00:25,967
[100% competitive, YOHAN]
Nice! YOHAN! Show us! Show us!

21
00:00:25,968 --> 00:00:27,100
I’m in my prime these days.

22
00:00:27,101 --> 00:00:28,297
[The golden youngest, JISUNG]
JISUNG, the man with two hearts!

23
00:00:28,297 --> 00:00:29,334
JISUNG’s really good at this.

24
00:00:29,334 --> 00:00:31,113
"ALL or NOTHING".

25
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,867
[What will they do in this place?]

26
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,733
[Depending on the mission results]

27
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:38,767
[The princes indulge in luxury]
Whoa, this place is so luxurious!

28
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:39,501
This is so great.

29
00:00:39,502 --> 00:00:40,400
Wow, I’m getting goosebumps.

30
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,067
[And the paupers lose it all...]
I don’t wanna be a pauper.

31
00:00:42,068 --> 00:00:43,085
What am I supposed
to do if I end up a pauper?

32
00:00:43,086 --> 00:00:44,000
I don’t think I can be a pauper…

33
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,600
["ALL or NOTHING" First Mission: The Pharaoh’s Table]
Will we become a prince or a pauper?

34
00:00:46,832 --> 00:00:49,065
[After eating everything and clearing the plates]
We just have to eat well and finish the chosen courses.

35
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:51,333
[at the restaurants reserved in order]
Yes, it’s delicious.

36
00:00:51,334 --> 00:00:51,900
It's good!

37
00:00:51,901 --> 00:00:53,200
- It's good?
- Yeah!

38
00:00:53,201 --> 00:00:54,420
[The first team to reach the meetup spot wins!]
The first team that gets

39
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,933
to the meetup spot wins.

40
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,684
[A total of 7 reserved locations]
We don’t know which is

41
00:00:58,691 --> 00:01:00,973
dessert, meat, or seafood here.

42
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:03,300
[Depending on their decisions]
I was hoping the restaurants were all close by.

43
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,433
[Today’s fate]
I hope they're nearby.

44
00:01:04,434 --> 00:01:05,533
[will be decided]
I want to go somewhere close.

45
00:01:05,534 --> 00:01:06,833
[I'll decide my own fate]
No!

46
00:01:06,834 --> 00:01:08,333
- Nice!
- Good job!

47
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:10,933
[There's no way I'm being a pauper…!]
Good job! YOHAN! Nice!

48
00:01:10,934 --> 00:01:11,700
Alright, here we go!

49
00:01:11,701 --> 00:01:13,300
[And the battle officially begins!]
Let’s go!

50
00:01:13,586 --> 00:01:14,905
[Food first, battle later]
Wow, this is amazing.

51
00:01:14,905 --> 00:01:15,600
It smells delicious.

52
00:01:15,905 --> 00:01:17,600
[A feast of food unfolds before them]
Wow! The view is amazing!!

53
00:01:17,601 --> 00:01:18,533
This is seriously good!

54
00:01:18,534 --> 00:01:20,515
[Digging in without hesitation]
It tastes amazing.

55
00:01:20,515 --> 00:01:21,300
This is really tasty.

56
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,867
[With the younger members stepping up]
JISUNG, you really eat fast.

57
00:01:22,868 --> 00:01:24,067
You're really eating well today.

58
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:25,967
[The first course gets cleared in no time]
Wow!

59
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:28,467
[The long-awaited moment
of choosing the second restaurant]

60
00:01:28,468 --> 00:01:29,466
[Team LEETEUK ends up at a nearby restaurant]
It's somewhere close, LEETEUK.

61
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:30,967
- Hey, it's right nearby! Let's go!
- We're good, we're good! Let's go!

62
00:01:30,968 --> 00:01:31,500
Yeah.

63
00:01:31,501 --> 00:01:33,533
[Team SHINDONG gets stuck at a restaurant far away]
Oh, it's the farthest!

64
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:38,033
[What will be their fate…?]

65
00:01:38,034 --> 00:01:39,800
[CHAPTER.2]
[The one who sows the wind, reaps the storm]

66
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,405
[Team LEETEUK peacefully enjoys the meal]
I think it has curry powder and turmeric.

67
00:01:45,406 --> 00:01:47,000
- Oh!
- It does, right?

68
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:49,200
[A dark figure
slowly creeps up on them]

69
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,400
Who…are you?

70
00:01:51,603 --> 00:01:52,567
Who are you?

71
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:53,717
Oh, you scared me…!

72
00:01:54,897 --> 00:01:55,910
Oh, you scared me…!

73
00:01:56,933 --> 00:02:00,333
[Just earlier]
Seeing that we haven't taken the overpass…

74
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:02,700
[Team SHINDONG, who chose the other restaurant]
There are more foreign cars now.

75
00:02:02,701 --> 00:02:04,600
But I hope
the other team gets big portions.

76
00:02:04,601 --> 00:02:06,500
[Picked a place way too far away]

77
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:08,566
[Along with Cairo’s brutal rush hour]
This is when the traffic is heavy.

78
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:10,500
I see.

79
00:02:11,053 --> 00:02:14,526
Oh, we lost this.
What should we do?

80
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,300
[Team LEETEUK is almost done eating]

81
00:02:16,301 --> 00:02:18,298
[But they still haven't arrived yet]

82
00:02:18,299 --> 00:02:19,467
Ugh, this is bad.

83
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,267
[The gap keeps widening]
Should we hurry and use an item?

84
00:02:21,268 --> 00:02:24,633
[Will they just lose like this?]
I got so nervous that we might lose.

85
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:25,733
Oh, okay.

86
00:02:25,734 --> 00:02:26,506
[Let’s use an attack item]
Let's use it!

87
00:02:26,507 --> 00:02:28,166
- It's already hard deboning fish on your own.
- Yeah, you're right.

88
00:02:28,601 --> 00:02:30,200
YOHAN, can you read it out loud?
What does it say?

89
00:02:30,201 --> 00:02:32,600
"One hand's just for support"!

90
00:02:32,601 --> 00:02:33,067
Nice!

91
00:02:33,068 --> 00:02:34,267
[Used the attack item]
Ta-da!

92
00:02:34,268 --> 00:02:35,490
"One hand's just for support"!

93
00:02:35,491 --> 00:02:36,800
We will use it now.

94
00:02:37,167 --> 00:02:39,700
[Hehe]
Try deboning the fish with this!

95
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,167
Oh, it's done, it's done.

96
00:02:41,168 --> 00:02:43,000
- They have the same strategy as us!
- And on top of that…

97
00:02:43,001 --> 00:02:44,301
[JISUNG & JOHNNY get tied up]
LEETEUK, you don't have to tie your hands, right?

98
00:02:44,302 --> 00:02:45,500
Since we're on this side?

99
00:02:45,686 --> 00:02:47,480
Isn't it just
the two of us getting tied together?

100
00:02:47,481 --> 00:02:48,600
(Please lower your hand)
Am I getting tied too?

101
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:52,233
[Aha...!]
Am I getting tied too?

102
00:02:52,384 --> 00:02:54,277
[Chosen to get both hands tied]
Oh, I somehow ended up in the middle.

103
00:02:54,284 --> 00:02:55,697
- Should we do it like this, or that?
- I ended up being in the middle.

104
00:02:55,883 --> 00:02:58,187
[JISUNG’s hands get tightly tied]
Isn’t this something we should decide?

105
00:02:58,201 --> 00:03:00,433
Did you talk about
how to tie us together?

106
00:03:00,434 --> 00:03:05,200
[I’m supposed to be leading this game...!]
I need to take charge of this game, so…

107
00:03:05,201 --> 00:03:05,911
I'll go over there.

108
00:03:05,912 --> 00:03:06,967
And if you're...

109
00:03:06,968 --> 00:03:09,067
If you’re full, I’ll just eat it all.

110
00:03:09,068 --> 00:03:10,299
And if you're full…

111
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:11,900
[JISUNG, your hands are tied]
I’ll just eat it all.

112
00:03:11,901 --> 00:03:13,400
JISUNG.

113
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:17,867
[JISUNG, where’s your fork?]
Sit down, you sit.

114
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,600
Sit down, you sit.

115
00:03:19,890 --> 00:03:20,710
Sit down.

116
00:03:22,093 --> 00:03:24,360
[You take the lead]
Our JISUNG, open wide!

117
00:03:24,795 --> 00:03:26,522
Our JISUNG, open wide!

118
00:03:28,767 --> 00:03:29,801
[Somehow feeling like he misspoke]

119
00:03:29,802 --> 00:03:30,708
Whoa.

120
00:03:30,709 --> 00:03:31,700
Wow.

121
00:03:32,367 --> 00:03:33,200
Our JISUNG, open wide!

122
00:03:33,201 --> 00:03:34,067
Slowly, slowly!

123
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,067
LEETEUK, you're doing this
because you can't eat anymore, huh?

124
00:03:37,068 --> 00:03:39,133
[Bullseye]
No! I can still eat. I can.

125
00:03:39,134 --> 00:03:40,900
No, no! Just wait.

126
00:03:40,901 --> 00:03:41,880
I'm gonna eat.

127
00:03:41,881 --> 00:03:43,500
But please don't push yourself.

128
00:03:43,501 --> 00:03:45,100
No, I can eat, just watch.

129
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:47,800
JOHNNY is so cold.

130
00:03:48,067 --> 00:03:49,683
[I am?]
He's cold.

131
00:03:49,684 --> 00:03:50,290
Why’s that?

132
00:03:50,291 --> 00:03:53,033
[This guy]
He knows me way too well.

133
00:03:53,294 --> 00:03:55,897
[Unnecessarily romantic]
But LEETEUK, don't you think it's so romantic right now?

134
00:03:55,898 --> 00:03:59,233
[The beautifully flowing Nile River]
The Nile River right here...!

135
00:04:00,067 --> 00:04:02,067
[And our sweet LEETEUK...]
Our JISUNG, open wide!

136
00:04:02,068 --> 00:04:02,997
JISUNG, open wide!

137
00:04:02,998 --> 00:04:03,767
Slowly, slowly!

138
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:06,167
JISUNG, open wide!

139
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:11,600
I really love fish
that's been grilled

140
00:04:11,601 --> 00:04:13,167
with my favorite spices.

141
00:04:13,168 --> 00:04:14,700
So when that dish came out,
I enjoyed it a lot.

142
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:17,667
[Q. Did you get closer to LEETEUK?]
Did being tied up bring you two closer?

143
00:04:17,668 --> 00:04:20,300
I think it just
made us drift further apart.

144
00:04:20,713 --> 00:04:22,091
For the first time,
LEETEUK felt hard to…

145
00:04:22,092 --> 00:04:24,246
He felt harder…to approach, yes…

146
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,567
Oh, but hey…

147
00:04:25,568 --> 00:04:27,810
[The hard-to-approach
big bro has back pain]

148
00:04:27,811 --> 00:04:28,600
Oh, my back.

149
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,833
[Thud]

150
00:04:33,559 --> 00:04:36,001
[The type
that requires a lot of care]

151
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,367
I didn't get wet. I'm good.

152
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,367
LEETEUK, you could
just come over here.

153
00:04:40,368 --> 00:04:42,300
Oh, you're right.

154
00:04:42,301 --> 00:04:43,300
JOHNNY.

155
00:04:43,301 --> 00:04:44,600
As expected, JOHNNYUS.

156
00:04:44,601 --> 00:04:46,800
[With the high-maintenance big bro
and JOHNNYUS & JISUNG stepping up]

157
00:04:46,801 --> 00:04:49,133
It’s seriously tough
when your hands are tied.

158
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:51,500
[They ate without breaking a sweat]
Our JISUNG, open wide!

159
00:04:51,501 --> 00:04:52,933
Since there are no chopsticks here,

160
00:04:52,934 --> 00:04:54,204
I hope they debone
everything with their hands.

161
00:04:54,205 --> 00:04:55,000
Oh, that's nice.

162
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,667
[They used a fork like a pro]
Oh, I was gonna debone it.

163
00:04:58,059 --> 00:05:01,059
I really want LEETEUK
to sit right in the middle.

164
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:02,798
[Crushing even their tiniest hope]
Oh, JOHNNY! As expected!

165
00:05:02,799 --> 00:05:03,900
So neatly!

166
00:05:03,901 --> 00:05:07,033
We got lucky,
because we finished most of it,

167
00:05:07,034 --> 00:05:08,133
and there were no bones.

168
00:05:08,134 --> 00:05:11,233
It felt like
they were helping us win!

169
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:12,667
[Damage: 0]
We weren't affected at all.

170
00:05:12,933 --> 00:05:14,167
[After flawlessly blocking]
Will you show us your plate?

171
00:05:14,168 --> 00:05:16,233
[Team SHINDONG's attack]
I checked everything thoroughly.

172
00:05:16,433 --> 00:05:17,903
[Team LEETEUK clears the seafood course]
We're done!

173
00:05:17,904 --> 00:05:18,800
All done, finished!

174
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:21,000
- We really finished this one.
- Done!

175
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:24,200
[Just then,
SHINDONG makes a spy call]

176
00:05:24,201 --> 00:05:26,333
(We got a call!)

177
00:05:27,633 --> 00:05:29,033
Can they not answer it?

178
00:05:29,034 --> 00:05:30,867
Because their hands are tied up?

179
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:32,803
[They’re still blissfully unaware]
Maybe they can’t pick up because their hands are tied.

180
00:05:32,804 --> 00:05:34,067
LEETEUK!

181
00:05:34,567 --> 00:05:36,067
Nice to hear from you!

182
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:38,867
I know your hands
are tied right now.

183
00:05:38,868 --> 00:05:39,800
My hands?

184
00:05:39,801 --> 00:05:40,833
Yes.

185
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,200
We're tied up, you punk.

186
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:46,267
[So happy]

187
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:49,300
[Doing his best to appear
as hopeless as possible]

188
00:05:49,301 --> 00:05:50,233
But wait,

189
00:05:50,234 --> 00:05:52,233
are you still on the move?

190
00:05:52,234 --> 00:05:54,000
[Correct]
We’re still on the move.

191
00:05:54,467 --> 00:05:57,667
[WANGGEOZ are
happy on both sides]

192
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,467
It's so far…

193
00:06:00,926 --> 00:06:02,696
[Wrapping up the call]
Okay!

194
00:06:02,704 --> 00:06:04,233
Continue to enjoy your meal.

195
00:06:04,385 --> 00:06:05,805
Yes, we will.

196
00:06:06,005 --> 00:06:07,506
Thanks for the handcuffs.

197
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,433
Thank you.

198
00:06:08,853 --> 00:06:10,792
They think we haven’t eaten yet

199
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,800
We can take these off now, right?

200
00:06:11,801 --> 00:06:14,599
But there was nothing
on their plates when I looked.

201
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:17,100
- The food didn't come out yet.
- I guess they haven't opened up the food yet.

202
00:06:17,101 --> 00:06:18,733
Oh, this is easy!

203
00:06:18,734 --> 00:06:20,967
I'm gonna easily become a prince!

204
00:06:20,968 --> 00:06:22,697
While doing this program,

205
00:06:22,698 --> 00:06:24,467
I thought that
I'd take it easy and relax.

206
00:06:24,468 --> 00:06:26,367
[Grinning]

207
00:06:26,833 --> 00:06:27,700
[Team SHINDONG finally arrives
after the tour through Cairo]

208
00:06:27,701 --> 00:06:28,598
Huh?

209
00:06:28,599 --> 00:06:29,400
The smell is like…!

210
00:06:29,401 --> 00:06:30,193
Huh?

211
00:06:31,003 --> 00:06:31,767
SHINDONG.

212
00:06:31,768 --> 00:06:33,400
The pot is huge.

213
00:06:33,709 --> 00:06:35,491
Wait, what is this?

214
00:06:37,033 --> 00:06:39,333
[It's this far away, and the portions are huge?]
Oh wow, the smell is like…!

215
00:06:39,511 --> 00:06:41,298
[The bread (eish) appears again]
As expected, this is here too.

216
00:06:41,299 --> 00:06:43,500
- Oh!
- I guess you always wrap it with this here.

217
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,181
There are gloves for your hands.

218
00:06:46,182 --> 00:06:46,800
Huh?

219
00:06:47,088 --> 00:06:48,900
Oh, you're right.
I guess we're eating with our hands.

220
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:50,900
[What could possibly be inside?]
What is it?

221
00:06:50,901 --> 00:06:52,900
Wow, it's pretty big.

222
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,600
- Let’s open it right away.
- Okay.

223
00:06:54,601 --> 00:06:55,710
- First, it's warm. It's warm.
- Let's do it.

224
00:06:55,711 --> 00:06:56,633
- Oh, it's warm?
- Yes.

225
00:06:57,233 --> 00:06:59,884
[What dish is expensive in Korea, too?]
One, two, three!

226
00:06:59,885 --> 00:07:01,467
Okay, one two three!

227
00:07:03,195 --> 00:07:04,108
Huh?

228
00:07:04,288 --> 00:07:05,095
Oh.

229
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:06,767
- Ahahaha!
- Oh!

230
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,300
[Frozen]

231
00:07:08,301 --> 00:07:09,233
No, but wait…

232
00:07:09,234 --> 00:07:11,467
There's so much!

233
00:07:11,752 --> 00:07:12,988
[A huge pile of shrimp appears]
So much…!

234
00:07:12,997 --> 00:07:14,292
(Expensive)
There's so much!

235
00:07:14,294 --> 00:07:16,727
[Did Team LEETEUK use an attack item?]
Did they add a serving?

236
00:07:16,734 --> 00:07:18,467
[Nope]
They didn't for this?

237
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:21,400
This is jumbo...
grilled jumbo shrimp...

238
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:23,067
I’ve never seen
so many shrimp at once.

239
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:25,033
Even in Korea,
I don't eat that many.

240
00:07:25,133 --> 00:07:27,500
And Korea's known
for being generous with food.

241
00:07:27,501 --> 00:07:29,000
We don't eat shrimp like that.

242
00:07:29,001 --> 00:07:31,433
