717
00:23:19,967 --> 00:23:21,300
Wow, this restaurant…

718
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:23,733
Oh, there's something…

719
00:23:23,734 --> 00:23:26,100
different about it
from the other places.

720
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:30,933
[After pushing through
the bustling crowd]

721
00:23:31,767 --> 00:23:34,267
[Team SHINDONG arrives at the third restaurant]
Oh?

722
00:23:34,533 --> 00:23:36,967
[They arrived
way later than Team LEETEUK]

723
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,410
[But the portion looks small]
The portion size looks small.

724
00:23:38,411 --> 00:23:39,867
- I know, right?
- Right?

725
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:41,702
[Filled with the aroma of a famous restaurant]
And it smells so good.

726
00:23:41,703 --> 00:23:42,903
There are so many people here.

727
00:23:42,904 --> 00:23:44,133
They said
it's a really famous place.

728
00:23:45,033 --> 00:23:46,990
[The boiled meat for the meat course is…?]
Alright, here we go!

729
00:23:46,991 --> 00:23:48,867
One, two, three!

730
00:23:50,989 --> 00:23:52,000
- Huh?
- Huh?

731
00:23:53,197 --> 00:23:54,190
- Huh?
- Huh?

732
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:56,900
What is this...?

733
00:23:57,733 --> 00:24:00,167
[Chewy ox trotters]

734
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:02,767
[and ox knee cartilage
packed with rich collagen]

735
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:06,100
[slow-cooked with aromatic spices]

736
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:12,500
[A traditional
Egyptian health booster]

737
00:24:13,133 --> 00:24:15,067
[Kaware']

738
00:24:15,068 --> 00:24:17,667
[Small portion]

739
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,220
What is this...?

740
00:24:20,234 --> 00:24:23,333
[The dish feels somewhat like Korean food]
Doesn't it have a Korean vibe to it?

741
00:24:23,711 --> 00:24:24,897
This food…

742
00:24:24,898 --> 00:24:25,803
Is this the correct food?

743
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:29,000
Oh?! This seems delicious!

744
00:24:29,300 --> 00:24:30,000
Oh, wait, wait.

745
00:24:30,001 --> 00:24:31,100
What’s this?

746
00:24:31,101 --> 00:24:31,899
Oh, wait, wait.

747
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,404
[Suddenly, a tray appears]
What's this?

748
00:24:33,405 --> 00:24:35,166
- What's this?
- There's more?

749
00:24:37,663 --> 00:24:38,492
What's this?

750
00:24:38,501 --> 00:24:39,612
- What's this?
- Open it up.

751
00:24:41,593 --> 00:24:43,793
[It's me, the attack item]
The gentleman over there sent it.

752
00:24:43,801 --> 00:24:47,867
[So, it's finally arrived]
Ugh! Seriously!

753
00:24:49,701 --> 00:24:51,633
[A moment ago]
Should we do what we need to do?

754
00:24:52,233 --> 00:24:54,067
We'll use our item!

755
00:24:54,068 --> 00:24:56,467
"The gentleman over here sent it".

756
00:24:56,833 --> 00:24:57,917
…I think it's…"over there"…

757
00:24:57,918 --> 00:24:58,683
- Is it "over there"?
- Yeah.

758
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,214
[Anyway, attack item activated!]
Nice!

759
00:25:01,215 --> 00:25:02,900
Enjoy your meal!

760
00:25:03,768 --> 00:25:04,900
[You mean "finally"]
They "gladly" used it!

761
00:25:04,901 --> 00:25:06,199
Aw, man.

762
00:25:06,403 --> 00:25:08,900
[Start with the additional serving]
Please enjoy the first one they sent.

763
00:25:09,367 --> 00:25:10,733
Oh, the first one they sent…

764
00:25:10,734 --> 00:25:12,967
- I'll taste it first.
- Yeah, taste it first.

765
00:25:12,968 --> 00:25:14,533
[Light eater → Big eater]
[DAWN, who's changing up his image, goes first]

766
00:25:14,867 --> 00:25:16,733
But it's kind of
like ox bone soup.

767
00:25:16,734 --> 00:25:18,406
[Korean ox bone soup + a hint of curry...?]
It’s like ox bone soup with a hint of curry.

768
00:25:18,406 --> 00:25:19,333
If you look here,

769
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:20,603
it’s kind of
like ox knee soup!

770
00:25:20,604 --> 00:25:22,000
- Oh, not bad.
- Right?

771
00:25:22,404 --> 00:25:23,700
Yeah, I think it's gonna be good.

772
00:25:23,967 --> 00:25:26,500
[KIM YOHAN]
[On an intermittent fast (1 hour completed)]

773
00:25:27,115 --> 00:25:28,022
Oh, the smell!

774
00:25:28,023 --> 00:25:30,102
Yeah, it smells
very savory and rich.

775
00:25:36,333 --> 00:25:37,984
[Say something, please]

776
00:25:37,985 --> 00:25:38,967
Is it okay?

777
00:25:38,968 --> 00:25:39,533
It's really good!

778
00:25:39,534 --> 00:25:40,600
- Really?
- Yeah.

779
00:25:40,601 --> 00:25:42,300
Then, we can eat this, right?

780
00:25:42,301 --> 00:25:43,692
[After finishing the attack item, the game resumes]
You have to finish one bowl first.

781
00:25:43,693 --> 00:25:45,494
Oh, really?
Hey, you need to eat faster, then.

782
00:25:45,495 --> 00:25:46,400
Yeah, it can't be helped.

783
00:25:46,401 --> 00:25:47,600
- What?
- Hey, you have to eat quickly!

784
00:25:47,886 --> 00:25:50,307
- Try some…!
- No, you dipped your spoon in it,

785
00:25:50,308 --> 00:25:52,283
- so you eat it first.
- But you really need to try a spoonful.

786
00:25:52,284 --> 00:25:53,704
- Oh, really?
- Yes, really.

787
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:56,367
[To match the wait]

788
00:25:56,368 --> 00:25:58,100
[A big spoonful]

789
00:25:59,501 --> 00:26:00,194
Hmm?

790
00:26:00,933 --> 00:26:02,200
It's good, right?

791
00:26:02,201 --> 00:26:03,633
It doesn't have a smell at all!

792
00:26:03,634 --> 00:26:05,400
It doesn't have
that gamey meat smell.

793
00:26:06,411 --> 00:26:07,200
This is so good!

794
00:26:07,201 --> 00:26:09,800
[A rich broth simmered for hours]
Oh, now I get why this place is famous

795
00:26:09,801 --> 00:26:11,704
[with a chewy, savory texture that melts in your mouth]
Koreans will definitely love this.

796
00:26:11,711 --> 00:26:14,473
- It'd go well with alcohol.
- But it's slightly mild.

797
00:26:14,603 --> 00:26:16,467
I think it's a bit
mild for us to eat.

798
00:26:16,468 --> 00:26:17,300
Mmm! Mhm!

799
00:26:17,301 --> 00:26:18,700
Oh?! Hmm?!

800
00:26:18,701 --> 00:26:19,567
[Wait, what?!]

801
00:26:19,826 --> 00:26:21,526
It's delicious!

802
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:24,000
[And then...]
Are you full?

803
00:26:25,193 --> 00:26:26,700
[Gulping it down as the leader]

804
00:26:26,701 --> 00:26:28,426
It's really delicious.

805
00:26:30,233 --> 00:26:32,200
[Cleared the extra serving attack item!]

806
00:26:32,201 --> 00:26:34,515
[Victory vibes are kicking in!]
But honestly, this much food is…

807
00:26:34,516 --> 00:26:35,499
Hey, if we eat fast,

808
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:37,000
I think we can
turn the tables at this rate!

809
00:26:37,133 --> 00:26:38,718
[The game starts now!]
Hey, we can totally turn this around.

810
00:26:38,718 --> 00:26:39,834
This is…Hey.

811
00:26:39,834 --> 00:26:42,800
[Let’s really hit the gas!]
Oh, this will be gone in no time, but…

812
00:26:47,833 --> 00:26:48,467
Ugh…

813
00:26:49,567 --> 00:26:50,800
[Attack item activated]
They used a mission.

814
00:26:50,801 --> 00:26:52,633
Oh, come on!

815
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,900
They're using them all here...

816
00:26:54,901 --> 00:26:55,633
Ugh!

817
00:26:55,634 --> 00:26:57,199
[Even used their last attack card]
That traditional coin game!

818
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,500
[The traditional coin game]
We'll send one more your way!

819
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:01,467
Let's hit them hard
with one big blow!

820
00:27:01,533 --> 00:27:02,700
[Fed up]

821
00:27:02,701 --> 00:27:03,933
No, like…

822
00:27:04,100 --> 00:27:06,267
It's just evil.

823
00:27:06,268 --> 00:27:08,200
It's so mean…

824
00:27:08,967 --> 00:27:10,110
[RULE]
[Flip all 6 coins at once]

825
00:27:10,111 --> 00:27:11,033
Let's be quick with it.

826
00:27:11,281 --> 00:27:12,233
Just try it out.

827
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:14,567
[Carefully]
Oh, my hands are so...

828
00:27:14,568 --> 00:27:16,700
[Getting into position]
small.

829
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:23,533
Hey, how long
is this gonna take…

830
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:26,100
Just hit it a few times!

831
00:27:26,101 --> 00:27:27,833
You can just
quickly do it a few times...

832
00:27:30,867 --> 00:27:32,833
[No flip]

833
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:35,167
Oh, this is bad…

834
00:27:36,633 --> 00:27:38,633
Oh, this is really bad.

835
00:27:38,634 --> 00:27:40,100
What are we gonna do about this?

836
00:27:40,297 --> 00:27:41,903
Can we even get the hang of it?

837
00:27:43,333 --> 00:27:44,800
[Super stuck]

838
00:27:44,801 --> 00:27:46,700
Hey, this is seriously bad.

839
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:50,827
[Will they make it out by today…?]
Hey hey, wait a sec. So this… So…

840
00:27:51,067 --> 00:27:53,167
[And the issue here is]

841
00:27:53,633 --> 00:27:56,067
[They're slowing down
because they're stuffed]

842
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:02,000
No, I'll eat that, I'm fine.

843
00:28:02,001 --> 00:28:02,833
Oh!

844
00:28:02,834 --> 00:28:03,800
You should still give it a try.

845
00:28:03,801 --> 00:28:04,467
You want me to eat this?

846
00:28:04,468 --> 00:28:06,033
No, I'm gonna eat
another one of those.

847
00:28:06,034 --> 00:28:07,333
Oh, but still!

848
00:28:07,334 --> 00:28:08,309
[Brotherly love blooms through the fullness]
No, no.

849
00:28:08,310 --> 00:28:09,095
LEETEUK!

850
00:28:09,096 --> 00:28:11,409
- Good food is… Oh!
- Don't lose your sense of romance!

851
00:28:11,410 --> 00:28:13,066
Oof! Romance!
Romance Bro, you first.

852
00:28:13,067 --> 00:28:15,266
[Little bro, you first]
No, seriously, I’m good.

853
00:28:15,268 --> 00:28:16,097
[Big bro, you first]
You should try it once.

854
00:28:16,098 --> 00:28:18,133
Wait, I'm eating!
It's right here!

855
00:28:18,501 --> 00:28:19,333
Right here, see?

856
00:28:19,334 --> 00:28:20,233
Open wide!

857
00:28:20,234 --> 00:28:21,933
No.

858
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,700
Can you cut it smaller?

859
00:28:23,701 --> 00:28:25,000
Please slice it for me.

860
00:28:25,300 --> 00:28:26,100
It's too big.

861
00:28:26,101 --> 00:28:28,167
[A true class act
can smile through the fullness]

862
00:28:32,333 --> 00:28:34,600
It's been 3 hours and 42 minutes
since we started eating.

863
00:28:35,033 --> 00:28:37,133
No, like…

864
00:28:37,134 --> 00:28:39,367
We were told
to enjoy a trip in Egypt,

865
00:28:39,368 --> 00:28:41,500
but it feels like
all we'll see is the tabletop.

866
00:28:41,933 --> 00:28:43,883
[Not a magic carpet]
Honestly…

867
00:28:43,884 --> 00:28:46,496
[Traveling in Egypt by dining table...]
I wonder if I even saw Egypt.

868
00:28:46,497 --> 00:28:47,533
Right?

869
00:28:47,900 --> 00:28:50,833
[Still]
The most important part of travel is food...!

870
00:28:50,834 --> 00:28:51,967
- Right.
- That's right, that's right.

871
00:28:51,968 --> 00:28:54,100
[A class act, for sure]

872
00:28:54,167 --> 00:28:55,667
Let's quickly eat and go!

873
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:57,433
I'll eat one of those…

874
00:28:57,434 --> 00:28:58,667
I'll also have one of these.

875
00:28:58,900 --> 00:29:00,316
[Soon, the bottom of the plate starts showing]
I think it's the first time in my life

876
00:29:00,317 --> 00:29:01,767
that I've eaten this much.

877
00:29:01,768 --> 00:29:03,300
Then JISUNG, you take a break.

878
00:29:03,301 --> 00:29:04,900
I'll finish all of this too!

879
00:29:06,167 --> 00:29:10,400
[Eating it all on his own]
I need to take charge of this game!

880
00:29:11,633 --> 00:29:14,033
[With the youngest
filling up his cheeks,]

881
00:29:14,433 --> 00:29:17,100
[the older brothers
put on a final spurt too]

882
00:29:17,101 --> 00:29:18,093
(One last piece)

883
00:29:18,094 --> 00:29:19,400
- Yes, I will…
- Okay.

884
00:29:19,567 --> 00:29:21,233
[Popped it in!]

885
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:24,467
[Team LEETEUK clears the grilled meat course!]
Did you already eat it?

886
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:26,567
But, you know,
we finished everything, right?

887
00:29:26,568 --> 00:29:28,400
We just need to go!
After making one call!

888
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:32,200
(Trying to fish for their location)

889
00:29:35,133 --> 00:29:35,967
No way...

890
00:29:35,968 --> 00:29:36,600
LEETEUK...!

891
00:29:36,601 --> 00:29:37,867
Yes?

892
00:29:38,733 --> 00:29:41,333
Why are you
sending so many missions?

893
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:43,833
You promised not to do this…

894
00:29:43,900 --> 00:29:46,233
[We did?]
Why, why, why?

895
00:29:47,100 --> 00:29:48,600
Are you playing the game?

896
00:29:48,933 --> 00:29:51,033
We're not able to eat the food!

897
00:29:51,267 --> 00:29:53,309
That must be so fun!

898
00:29:53,310 --> 00:29:54,316
Come on.

899
00:29:55,533 --> 00:29:56,267
That's right!

900
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,000
That's right!

901
00:29:58,892 --> 00:30:00,218
(Phone call on hold)
We just need to flip one more.

902
00:30:00,219 --> 00:30:01,803
- Just need to flip that one.
- Just flip that last one.

903
00:30:01,804 --> 00:30:02,825
One?

904
00:30:02,826 --> 00:30:05,192
[The worst phone etiquette]
What's the head and what's the tail?

905
00:30:05,201 --> 00:30:06,900
So, this is one,
and this is one…

906
00:30:06,901 --> 00:30:09,667
[But… Wait…]

907
00:30:09,668 --> 00:30:10,400
That's right!

908
00:30:10,401 --> 00:30:12,185
[They're not that far off]
Oh, we don't have time to watch this!

909
00:30:12,186 --> 00:30:13,467
LEETEUK, hang up!

910
00:30:13,793 --> 00:30:15,226
[If they flip the coin,
they’ll catch up in a flash]

911
00:30:15,234 --> 00:30:15,888
No, like…

912
00:30:15,889 --> 00:30:16,867
We're done!
Let's just go!

913
00:30:16,868 --> 00:30:17,708
We're in big trouble.

914
00:30:17,709 --> 00:30:19,733
Yeah. Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

915
00:30:19,933 --> 00:30:22,566
[Meanwhile, this side’s also in big trouble]
Hey, we're in trouble, this is bad.

916
00:30:22,567 --> 00:30:25,033
I think the pumping is important here!

917
00:30:25,034 --> 00:30:27,300
Yeah, pump it up.
Pump it a lot!

918
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:29,567
Are there no cheap tricks
or anything like that for this?

919
00:30:29,568 --> 00:30:31,033
But flipping 6 coins…

920
00:30:31,034 --> 00:30:34,800
[A big amount: 600 won]
I never tried it, because I didn't have enough money.

921
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,067
[KIM YOHAN]
[Personal Best: 5 coins]

922
00:30:37,567 --> 00:30:39,967
[Get into position]

923
00:30:42,667 --> 00:30:43,933
That's it!
Hey, you got it!

924
00:30:43,934 --> 00:30:44,967
- Oh! It's like this!
- It's this kind of vibe! Hey! Hey!

925
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:46,790
[The epitome of character growth]
Again, again, again!

926
00:30:46,791 --> 00:30:48,033
I think it'll flip,
if I do it a bit more gently.

927
00:30:48,733 --> 00:30:50,833
One person, keep doing it!
One person should keep doing it!

928
00:30:50,834 --> 00:30:52,267
[YOHAN, let's go!]
Oof, I'm burping here.

929
00:30:52,268 --> 00:30:54,233
[Cheering straight from the gut]

930
00:30:54,234 --> 00:30:55,867
[YOHAN's relentless challenge continues]

931
00:30:57,133 --> 00:30:58,800
[Change 6 heads]

932
00:30:58,801 --> 00:31:00,967
[To tails]

933
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:03,933
- That's it!
- Oh!

934
00:31:04,990 --> 00:31:06,100
- That's it!
- Oh!

935
00:31:06,101 --> 00:31:08,300
[Two heads left]

936
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:09,567
Two! Two!

937
00:31:09,568 --> 00:31:10,899
- Oh, okay!
- I'll flip it for you!

938
00:31:10,900 --> 00:31:11,967
Be gentle with it! Be gentle.

939
00:31:11,968 --> 00:31:14,133
[Let's continue with YOHAN's lucky streak!]
You just keep going. Just you alone.

940
00:31:14,733 --> 00:31:15,567
I'll flip them quickly.

941
00:31:16,733 --> 00:31:19,600
[Attempting right away!]

942
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:20,800
- Oh!
- That's it!

943
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,990
Ugh…Two! Two!!

944
00:31:25,991 --> 00:31:27,400
It's two every time.
Again, again, again!

945
00:31:27,667 --> 00:31:29,367
Just keep doing it!
Keep doing it! Just do it!

946
00:31:29,467 --> 00:31:31,667
[Fourth attempt right away]

947
00:31:36,167 --> 00:31:38,667
[Head → Tail]
[They all flipped…?]

948
00:31:39,533 --> 00:31:41,433
[One head left]

949
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:43,233
One! One! One!

950
00:31:43,733 --> 00:31:45,800
[Coin…You're driving us crazy…]
One, one! Again, again, again!

951
00:31:46,267 --> 00:31:47,467
Wow,
but this is looking promising!

952
00:31:47,468 --> 00:31:48,233
I feel like we'll get it!

953
00:31:48,330 --> 00:31:50,612
[Changing it up to Tail → Head]
I feel like we'll get it!

954
00:31:50,612 --> 00:31:51,534
My hands are too small.

955
00:31:51,933 --> 00:31:53,667
No, you can do it!
You've got this!

956
00:31:54,100 --> 00:31:56,400
[Goal: 6 heads]

957
00:32:01,500 --> 00:32:03,683
[Anxiously stomping his feet]
One! One! Wow…!

958
00:32:03,684 --> 00:32:05,400
Wow, this is making me mad.

959
00:32:05,401 --> 00:32:06,700
[So close]
One each time… Wow…

960
00:32:06,933 --> 00:32:09,567
[To make things worse, the food's cooling down]
No, we're gonna get it soon.

961
00:32:09,568 --> 00:32:11,800
[Team LEETEUK only has one more destination left]
There's only one place for dessert.

962
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:14,400
[About 50 minutes]
It's from one end to the other.

963
00:32:14,401 --> 00:32:16,267
[The distance is the problem]
It's probably gonna take us an hour.

964
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,995
[After tying up the other team
with an attack item, they take off]

965
00:32:18,996 --> 00:32:20,167
Oof!

966
00:32:20,654 --> 00:32:21,700
Let’s go!

967
00:32:21,701 --> 00:32:22,898
[CLEAR, CLEAR, Meat, Dessert]

968
00:32:22,899 --> 00:32:24,798
[Team LEETEUK's To-Do: Move locations (50 minutes)]
Hurry up, please!

969
00:32:24,799 --> 00:32:26,666
[Team SHINDONG's To-Do:
Flip Coins + Eat + Move locations (25 minutes)]

970
00:32:28,333 --> 00:32:29,100
Oh no, no, no!

971
00:32:29,101 --> 00:32:32,000
[The coin’s still being stubborn]
One! One, again! One! Wow!

972
00:32:32,326 --> 00:32:33,600
No, we'll get it soon.

973
00:32:33,601 --> 00:32:35,000
- We will, we will!
- It will happen!

974
00:32:35,609 --> 00:32:36,488
It'll happen, YOHAN!

975
00:32:36,708 --> 00:32:37,500
It will!

976
00:32:37,933 --> 00:32:39,867
That was too weak...

977
00:32:40,620 --> 00:32:41,594
Again, again.

978
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:45,733
[Everyone’s starting
to get anxious now]

979
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,500
...I have to do this, I have to.

980
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:52,233
[Carrying the burden
of the whole team]

981
00:32:53,300 --> 00:32:55,367
[One careful, decisive move]

982
00:32:55,633 --> 00:32:59,867
[Aiming for 6 heads this time too]

983
00:33:00,733 --> 00:33:02,367
[1. Head]

984
00:33:02,500 --> 00:33:04,200
[2. Head]

985
00:33:04,233 --> 00:33:05,967
[3. Head]

986
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:07,933
[4. Head]

987
00:33:07,934 --> 00:33:10,267
[5. Head]

988
00:33:11,867 --> 00:33:13,567
[Please...]

989
00:33:13,568 --> 00:33:17,533
[Just flip…]

990
00:33:19,033 --> 00:33:22,033
[The last coin is...]

991
00:33:22,034 --> 00:33:23,900
[Head]

992
00:33:24,300 --> 00:33:26,833
[ALL CLEAR]

993
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:28,897
WE GOT IT!!

994
00:33:29,533 --> 00:33:31,067
[We…]
WE GOT IT!!

995
00:33:31,068 --> 00:33:33,800
[Got it]
Okay, we're good!

996
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:36,367
[Let’s go now!]
We're good! Eat, eat, eat! We're good!

997
00:33:36,368 --> 00:33:38,433
Eat up, eat up!

998
00:33:38,434 --> 00:33:39,500
Once again…

999
00:33:39,933 --> 00:33:41,667
The ace always
shows up at times like this…

1000
00:33:41,668 --> 00:33:42,933
YOHAN…!

1001
00:33:42,934 --> 00:33:45,267
[KIM YOHAN / Personal best: 6 coins]
"Hmm? I think I should nudge it a bit."

1002
00:33:45,268 --> 00:33:46,667
"I don't think I should hit too hard."

1003
00:33:46,668 --> 00:33:47,626
As I was doing it,

1004
00:33:47,627 --> 00:33:49,467
I was able to get
the hang of it pretty quickly.

1005
00:33:50,233 --> 00:33:51,410
[Hehehehehe]

1006
00:33:51,411 --> 00:33:53,500
Why is the chunk
of meat in mine so big?

1007
00:33:53,501 --> 00:33:54,600
Hehe, this...

1008
00:33:54,601 --> 00:33:55,267
actually…

1009
00:33:55,268 --> 00:33:56,967
worked! Ohahaha!

1010
00:33:57,100 --> 00:33:58,085
[Still proud thinking about it]

1011
00:33:58,086 --> 00:33:59,333
Oh, the gelatin!

1012
00:33:59,433 --> 00:34:00,310
[Only three bowls of Kaware' left!]

1013
00:34:00,311 --> 00:34:01,567
Oh, I’m so full, what do I do?

1014
00:34:04,609 --> 00:34:05,509
YOHAN, you've got this!

1015
00:34:05,702 --> 00:34:06,566
We can't lose.

1016
00:34:07,116 --> 00:34:07,933
Hey, if we finish this,

1017
00:34:07,934 --> 00:34:09,000
I think we can win!

1018
00:34:09,001 --> 00:34:10,600
They went really far out.

1019
00:34:10,768 --> 00:34:12,500
They were still
at the restaurant, too.

1020
00:34:13,200 --> 00:34:16,733
[But Team LEETEUK is now on the move]
Today was not bad, not bad at all.

1021
00:34:17,333 --> 00:34:19,733
There was just too much lamb…

1022
00:34:20,033 --> 00:34:23,900
[Team LEETEUK is just as anxious]
The portion size was way bigger than expected.

1023
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:27,800
[Let's eat quickly and catch up!]

1024
00:34:28,293 --> 00:34:29,897
Oh, we're properly
nourishing our bodies today.

1025
00:34:32,867 --> 00:34:34,600
[Amazed]

1026
00:34:34,601 --> 00:34:35,600
Guys, keep it up!

1027
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:37,200
We’re almost there!

1028
00:34:39,193 --> 00:34:42,526
[Rising Food Fighter DAWN clears his bowl]
Wow!

1029
00:34:42,694 --> 00:34:46,193
[And Food Fighter YOHAN, as well]
YOHAN, almost there! Just hang in a bit more.

1030
00:34:46,201 --> 00:34:47,007
You're doing great.

1031
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:50,733
I think it came
back up a little just now.

1032
00:34:50,967 --> 00:34:52,833
[Hnng…]

1033
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:57,300
[Nourishing his body until the end]

1034
00:34:58,233 --> 00:34:59,685
[Team SHINDONG:
Meat course with boiled meat, CLEARED!]

1035
00:34:59,686 --> 00:35:00,983
Okay, can we head out now?

1036
00:35:00,984 --> 00:35:02,895
[Time to head to dessert]
Dessert? There’s only one spot for it, right?

1037
00:35:02,896 --> 00:35:03,533
Okay!

1038
00:35:03,534 --> 00:35:04,919
[Quickly checking the map]

1039
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:06,967
Yeah, there’s just one place left.

1040
00:35:06,968 --> 00:35:07,709
[About 25 minutes]
We were here.

1041
00:35:07,709 --> 00:35:09,007
Here, here.
We have to head here now, right?

1042
00:35:09,007 --> 00:35:09,900
Okay.

1043
00:35:09,901 --> 00:35:10,701
Compared to coming from here,

1044
00:35:10,701 --> 00:35:11,517
[Around 50 minutes]
we're way faster.

1045
00:35:11,518 --> 00:35:12,567
- Let's go, let's go.
- Yeah, way faster, for sure.

1046
00:35:12,568 --> 00:35:14,433
Let's hurry!
We can win this!

1047
00:35:14,434 --> 00:35:15,267
[Around 25 minutes]
[Around 50 minutes]

1048
00:35:15,268 --> 00:35:17,467
[Team SHINDONG heads out late,
but is closer to the location]

1049
00:35:18,233 --> 00:35:21,800
[Meanwhile,
Team LEETEUK is already on the move]

1050
00:35:22,033 --> 00:35:23,609
[Can Team SHINDONG…]
We’re heading out!

1051
00:35:23,610 --> 00:35:25,567
[turn this situation around…?]
To the next location!

1052
00:35:25,733 --> 00:35:29,400
[Everyone heads to the final meetup place]
Ugh, I’m so full.

1053
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,700
But honestly, today…

1054
00:35:31,900 --> 00:35:34,033
[Out of nowhere]
I had so much fun doing this with you guys.

1055
00:35:34,167 --> 00:35:35,233
Heh…!

1056
00:35:35,367 --> 00:35:37,967
[Why would you say that already?]
You kinda said it like we already lost.

1057
00:35:38,433 --> 00:35:40,406
[During the long ride]
But our vibe is completely different

1058
00:35:40,407 --> 00:35:42,766
[their confidence fades]
going there and coming back.

1059
00:35:43,267 --> 00:35:45,233
But did JOHNNY pick
everything today?

1060
00:35:45,500 --> 00:35:46,633
But…

1061
00:35:48,900 --> 00:35:50,896
[This romantic soul clings onto hope]
We honestly won.

1062
00:35:50,897 --> 00:35:52,292
Yeah, we won.

1063
00:35:52,301 --> 00:35:53,318
[What are you even saying?]
Won, exactly how?

1064
00:35:53,319 --> 00:35:54,967
Oh, so I mean…

1065
00:35:54,968 --> 00:35:58,167
It’s just that
the situation wasn’t on our side...

1066
00:35:58,693 --> 00:36:00,610
[Romantic human]
It’s all about romance, you know.

1067
00:36:00,611 --> 00:36:01,660
Romance?

1068
00:36:01,668 --> 00:36:03,933
[Romance copier]
It's romantic just being here.

1069
00:36:03,934 --> 00:36:05,097
But first,

1070
00:36:05,098 --> 00:36:07,800
I do think that
we're heading back defeated.

1071
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:11,633
[Suddenly back to reality]
We shouldn’t have chased romance...

1072
00:36:11,634 --> 00:36:13,300
No.

1073
00:36:13,301 --> 00:36:16,267
We came
all the way to Egypt, after all.

1074
00:36:16,368 --> 00:36:18,167
JOHNNY, you seem like
you have a split personality right now.

1075
00:36:18,733 --> 00:36:21,633
So, our choices were solid
up to the second course.

1076
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,984
[If only JOHNNYUS' luck]
Until the end,

1077
00:36:23,985 --> 00:36:26,333
[stayed with us…]
if we had picked boiled meat,

1078
00:36:26,793 --> 00:36:28,197
we would've
arrived 1-2 hours earlier.

1079
00:36:28,198 --> 00:36:28,803
Wow.

1080
00:36:28,804 --> 00:36:29,710
Right?

1081
00:36:29,711 --> 00:36:30,493
That's right.

1082
00:36:30,501 --> 00:36:32,467
But I'll say it again.

1083
00:36:32,468 --> 00:36:34,567
[Only romance]
I only made the romantic choices.

1084
00:36:34,700 --> 00:36:35,833
Nice.

1085
00:36:35,834 --> 00:36:37,367
[Staff]
Can you do an acrostic with "Romance"?

1086
00:36:37,667 --> 00:36:39,967
"Rom".

1087
00:36:39,968 --> 00:36:41,333
[Rom: Following romance]
"Following romance."

1088
00:36:41,334 --> 00:36:43,333
"Ance".

1089
00:36:43,334 --> 00:36:45,833
[Ance: …is all I did…]
"…is all I did…"

1090
00:36:46,226 --> 00:36:48,596
I really hope we win
after saying all that.

1091
00:36:48,604 --> 00:36:49,467
Seriously.

1092
00:36:49,468 --> 00:36:50,500
Then I'd be tearing up.

1093
00:36:50,501 --> 00:36:52,133
But honestly,

1094
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:56,784
we are clinging to
that 1% chance of winning.

1095
00:36:57,067 --> 00:36:59,034
[Wishful thinking kicks in again]
We keep saying we lost, but hey, you never know.

1096
00:36:59,034 --> 00:37:01,626
- There's a thing called "You never know."
- It's like, "You never know."

1097
00:37:01,634 --> 00:37:04,933
[Lights OFF]

1098
00:37:05,033 --> 00:37:06,067
[Self-OUT]

1099
00:37:06,068 --> 00:37:07,707
[Darkness is needed for the leader's tears]
I felt like I was gonna cry…

1100
00:37:07,708 --> 00:37:11,191
I felt like I was gonna cry,
so I turned it off.

1101
00:37:11,267 --> 00:37:11,933
Okay.

1102
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:14,200
[Following LEETEUK's example, OUT]

1103
00:37:14,433 --> 00:37:16,833
[Lights ON]
So, did we

1104
00:37:16,834 --> 00:37:17,967
become princes

1105
00:37:17,968 --> 00:37:20,100
or paupers?

1106
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:22,767
[A broadcast-worthy performance]
Everyone, stay tuned for the reveal!

1107
00:37:23,167 --> 00:37:24,867
Nice.

1108
00:37:24,967 --> 00:37:28,300
They must be done eating
and on the way, right?

1109
00:37:28,301 --> 00:37:30,003
[CLEAR, CLEAR, CLEAR, Dessert]

1110
00:37:30,004 --> 00:37:32,633
Let's go for dessert!

1111
00:37:32,967 --> 00:37:34,933
It takes about 20 minutes, right?

1112
00:37:34,934 --> 00:37:36,533
Yeah, about that much.

1113
00:37:36,767 --> 00:37:38,800
I’m so curious...
Are they there?

1114
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:40,800
At this rate,
aren’t we basically the princes?

1115
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:43,500
But SHINDONG,
I've been thinking.

1116
00:37:43,867 --> 00:37:46,333
[Video call]
When LEETEUK called earlier,

1117
00:37:46,633 --> 00:37:47,800
what if they weren't
at the meat restaurant,

1118
00:37:47,801 --> 00:37:49,367
but the dessert place?

1119
00:37:49,633 --> 00:37:51,067
Huh? Already?

1120
00:37:51,068 --> 00:37:52,098
It could totally
be the dessert place

1121
00:37:52,099 --> 00:37:52,934
Because

1122
00:37:52,935 --> 00:37:55,133
(Fell asleep earlier)
we blacked out in the middle.

1123
00:37:55,134 --> 00:37:57,200
But if they were
at the dessert place…

1124
00:37:57,367 --> 00:38:00,233
If they finished eating the meat,
went to the dessert place,

1125
00:38:00,326 --> 00:38:02,702
and still gave us
an extra serving…

1126
00:38:02,703 --> 00:38:03,759
Ugh!

1127
00:38:03,967 --> 00:38:05,800
Then they're seriously the devil.

1128
00:38:05,867 --> 00:38:08,933
LEETEUK is a real devil.

1129
00:38:09,033 --> 00:38:11,800
Don't you get a feeling
they're hiding at the dessert place?

1130
00:38:11,926 --> 00:38:13,413
To get a shot of us
being really happy.

1131
00:38:13,414 --> 00:38:14,967
Ugh, that would be
the absolute worst.

1132
00:38:14,975 --> 00:38:17,574
If that happens,
it'd be so humiliating.

1133
00:38:17,967 --> 00:38:21,833
I think I can already
see LEETEUK's dimples.

1134
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:24,803
With his dimples
dipping in as he smiles.

1135
00:38:26,033 --> 00:38:28,300
Because everyone is lying,

1136
00:38:28,301 --> 00:38:30,233
you just can't believe anything!

1137
00:38:30,300 --> 00:38:31,967
Even during the video calls,

1138
00:38:32,533 --> 00:38:33,933
[Staring hard at the background]
the background behind them…!

1139
00:38:33,934 --> 00:38:36,600
That's all we have
to figure things out.

1140
00:38:36,833 --> 00:38:38,033
Everything that was said then

1141
00:38:38,034 --> 00:38:39,767
was a complete lie.

1142
00:38:40,233 --> 00:38:43,333
[Four hours into the mission]
[Current time: 21:20]

1143
00:38:43,704 --> 00:38:46,191
[Cairo, a city of incredible scale]
Egypt is really huge.

1144
00:38:46,192 --> 00:38:47,400
The city is.

1145
00:38:48,133 --> 00:38:49,584
[YOHAN] It's a horse!

1146
00:38:49,585 --> 00:38:50,498
The horse is running.

1147
00:38:50,499 --> 00:38:51,000
Wow.

1148
00:38:51,067 --> 00:38:53,667
[Cars and horses share the road]
Wow, there’s a horse-drawn carriage.

1149
00:38:53,867 --> 00:38:56,600
[Sunset brings Cairo alive]
It’s crazy how lively it is at this hour.

1150
00:38:56,900 --> 00:38:59,567
This place looks
really amazing. Wow!

1151
00:38:59,568 --> 00:39:02,567
[Luxury buildings appear]
What is this place? Why is it so fancy? Wow!

1152
00:39:03,167 --> 00:39:04,100
The hotel is really tall.

1153
00:39:04,101 --> 00:39:05,967
I want to sleep
somewhere like that…

1154
00:39:06,533 --> 00:39:09,200
The hot water probably
just pours out there, right…?

1155
00:39:09,433 --> 00:39:11,933
It'd be amazing
to wake up in a place like that.

1156
00:39:12,300 --> 00:39:14,103
[We really, really want to be princes]
If you compare this to Korea, it'd be like a Han River view.

1157
00:39:14,104 --> 00:39:16,167
Oh, you’re right.

1158
00:39:16,698 --> 00:39:18,600
There was that hotel
with a pyramid view, too

1159
00:39:18,806 --> 00:39:19,720
That's right.

1160
00:39:20,433 --> 00:39:21,833
[Back to reality]
Even if we end up as paupers today,

1161
00:39:21,834 --> 00:39:24,267
let's not complain
and just sleep well.

1162
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:26,867
[Losing it]

1163
00:39:26,967 --> 00:39:29,100
The mission was way too long.

1164
00:39:29,433 --> 00:39:32,333
Just coming to
Egypt was the mission.

1165
00:39:32,633 --> 00:39:35,700
I don't even think
Tom Cruise would do a mission this long.

1166
00:39:35,701 --> 00:39:37,933
And it’s still not over.

1167
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:40,133
I think I'd be fine
with being a pauper today.

1168
00:39:40,134 --> 00:39:40,967
Because for today,

1169
00:39:40,968 --> 00:39:41,900
[Sleepy paupers]
all we have to do is sleep.

1170
00:39:41,901 --> 00:39:43,567
[Full paupers]
We finished eating all the food.

1171
00:39:43,568 --> 00:39:46,000
[Grateful paupers]
I'd just be thankful to sleep.

1172
00:39:46,067 --> 00:39:48,900
[Finding silver linings as a pauper while feeling anxious]
Hey, but pauper clothes might be more comfortable.

1173
00:39:49,167 --> 00:39:50,700
I like the pauper life.

1174
00:39:50,733 --> 00:39:53,400
I like v…vintage...

1175
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:56,866
I'm saying this now,
but if we become princes, I'd be the happiest ever.

1176
00:39:57,100 --> 00:39:58,933
But can I tell you something?

1177
00:39:59,033 --> 00:40:01,233
We're feeling this way now,

1178
00:40:01,234 --> 00:40:02,885
[On the same wavelength]
and the other team is feeling the same way.

1179
00:40:02,886 --> 00:40:03,833
Right, right.

1180
00:40:04,567 --> 00:40:07,300
[They're seriously thinking the same thing]
Still, you never know. Let's not lose hope.

1181
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,867
I would be over the moon.

1182
00:40:09,868 --> 00:40:11,200
- If we win, seriously…
- Yeah, I'd be so happy.

1183
00:40:11,201 --> 00:40:13,600
[Overjoyed at the thought of being a prince]
I might even seriously cry.

1184
00:40:13,933 --> 00:40:15,100
If I really become
a prince today,

1185
00:40:15,101 --> 00:40:16,167
when you guys
make your comeback,

1186
00:40:16,168 --> 00:40:17,967
I’m sending you a coffee truck.

1187
00:40:18,093 --> 00:40:20,060
[A prince's promise]
[A heartfelt coffee truck gift]

1188
00:40:20,068 --> 00:40:21,533
Because I’m so thankful to you guys.

1189
00:40:21,534 --> 00:40:23,667
[Team Prince, let's go!]
Like, "Team Prince! Let's go!"

1190
00:40:23,700 --> 00:40:25,933
[Who sent it is important]
"Sent by Prince SHINDONG"

1191
00:40:25,933 --> 00:40:27,800
Hahahahaha!

1192
00:40:27,933 --> 00:40:30,400
[Team SHINDONG,
who's getting closer]

1193
00:40:30,500 --> 00:40:33,100
[Team LEETEUK,
who finished eating and headed out first]

1194
00:40:33,167 --> 00:40:36,933
[A full-course dining race
shaped by their decisions]

1195
00:40:38,567 --> 00:40:41,733
They say baseball starts
at the bottom of the 9th with two outs.

1196
00:40:41,734 --> 00:40:42,900
The 9th inning magic.

1197
00:40:43,700 --> 00:40:46,800
Why am I suddenly
getting butterflies...!

1198
00:40:46,801 --> 00:40:48,433
I seriously hope
they're not there.

1199
00:40:48,633 --> 00:40:51,233
[Who will win the final course]
Please, please.

1200
00:40:51,234 --> 00:40:54,633
[to take it all?]
JISUNG’s hoping hard.

1201
00:40:54,967 --> 00:40:58,767
[Only the princes will enjoy]

1202
00:40:59,667 --> 00:41:03,000
