00:48:10,901 --> 00:48:11,867
We got it.
Hey, do it.

1441
00:48:12,067 --> 00:48:13,300
[Trying again before losing the groove]
Hey, YOHAN, go! YOHAN go!

1442
00:48:13,301 --> 00:48:15,800
- Just go, just go!
- Just go, just go!

1443
00:48:16,333 --> 00:48:17,200
Challenge accepted!

1444
00:48:17,700 --> 00:48:19,500
[YOHAN’s second attempt]

1445
00:48:24,233 --> 00:48:25,133
[Thud-Thunk]
Agh…!

1446
00:48:26,600 --> 00:48:28,233
This is driving me crazy! ACK!!!

1447
00:48:28,433 --> 00:48:30,133
I'll do it before you, SHINDONG.

1448
00:48:30,134 --> 00:48:31,700
[DAWN’s second attempt]
Challenge accepted! DAWN!

1449
00:48:31,701 --> 00:48:32,600
Challenge accepted!

1450
00:48:32,601 --> 00:48:33,667
Let’s do this!

1451
00:48:33,668 --> 00:48:34,900
[Casting a hopeful spell]
You could be the one to nail it.

1452
00:48:34,901 --> 00:48:35,900
That’s right, you got this!

1453
00:48:35,901 --> 00:48:37,067
Well, I mean, you think

1454
00:48:37,068 --> 00:48:38,633
[Self-doubt]
I would nail this?

1455
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:41,067
[Swish]

1456
00:48:41,068 --> 00:48:41,867
[Ding]
Agh!

1457
00:48:42,700 --> 00:48:43,600
Agh!

1458
00:48:43,601 --> 00:48:46,900
[Currently the best record]
[Success: 5 bottles, Fail: 1 bottle]

1459
00:48:47,167 --> 00:48:48,497
[Almost there now]
Ugh, seriously.

1460
00:48:48,498 --> 00:48:50,133
- Just do it, just do it!
- We're almost there, SHINDONG.

1461
00:48:50,134 --> 00:48:51,400
Wow, you had 5 standing…!

1462
00:48:51,401 --> 00:48:53,000
[Next up, SHINDONG]
I got it, I got it. I get it now.

1463
00:48:53,100 --> 00:48:54,900
[Team LEETEUK arrives!]

1464
00:48:55,600 --> 00:48:57,433
SHINDONG, you have to do it!

1465
00:48:57,700 --> 00:48:59,367
Is it here?

1466
00:48:59,667 --> 00:49:01,967
[SHINDONG’s second try]
Challenge accepted!

1467
00:49:02,200 --> 00:49:03,167
They're here! They're here!

1468
00:49:03,168 --> 00:49:04,290
They're here!
They're here! They're here!

1469
00:49:04,291 --> 00:49:05,700
- Wait, wait!
- Where? Where?

1470
00:49:06,233 --> 00:49:08,133
[Team LEETEUK]
But we should at least explain it to them.

1471
00:49:08,567 --> 00:49:09,800
[Curious]
What kind of game is this?

1472
00:49:09,801 --> 00:49:10,833
Alright, welcome!

1473
00:49:11,272 --> 00:49:12,606
Come this way!
This way, please!

1474
00:49:13,667 --> 00:49:14,983
Everyone, I’ve got good news.

1475
00:49:14,984 --> 00:49:15,600
Come quickly.

1476
00:49:15,601 --> 00:49:16,800
[What's there to be happy about?]
What good news do you have?

1477
00:49:16,801 --> 00:49:18,200
The game isn’t over yet.

1478
00:49:18,201 --> 00:49:19,000
Why? Why? Why?

1479
00:49:19,001 --> 00:49:20,672
[To Team LEETEUK]
The team that completes this mission first

1480
00:49:20,673 --> 00:49:21,667
[The final mission is announced]
wins the whole thing

1481
00:49:21,668 --> 00:49:22,500
We’ve been failing non-stop.

1482
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:24,500
You know when you pull this out?

1483
00:49:24,501 --> 00:49:25,700
So we came here first
and have been trying it, but…

1484
00:49:25,701 --> 00:49:26,600
[Dessert]
Aren’t we supposed to eat?

1485
00:49:26,601 --> 00:49:27,600
No, no.

1486
00:49:27,733 --> 00:49:30,600
[The final challenge for the dessert]
We have to do this to get dessert.

1487
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:32,767
[Processing the situation]
SHINDONG, how long have you been here?

1488
00:49:32,768 --> 00:49:34,308
[Lying without hesitation]
We've been here for like 30 minutes.

1489
00:49:34,309 --> 00:49:36,000
We got locked out
3 times already.

1490
00:49:36,233 --> 00:49:38,396
I'm getting hopeful!

1491
00:49:38,397 --> 00:49:39,922
[It's not the time to give up]
LEETEUK, it's not the end!

1492
00:49:39,923 --> 00:49:42,534
It's not over,
it's not over at all.

1493
00:49:42,534 --> 00:49:44,433
[Staff] Now that you’re here,

1494
00:49:44,434 --> 00:49:46,323
[No more 3-minute lockouts]
the 3-minute lockout has been removed,

1495
00:49:46,324 --> 00:49:47,402
- Oh, it's not a thing anymore?
- Yeah.

1496
00:49:47,403 --> 00:49:48,833
Oh, since they're here! Okay.

1497
00:49:49,100 --> 00:49:50,399
[The teams will take turns]
Each team will take turns

1498
00:49:50,400 --> 00:49:52,333
and try it one at a time.

1499
00:49:52,433 --> 00:49:54,567
Take turns? Okay.

1500
00:49:54,700 --> 00:49:56,133
After the team that succeeds

1501
00:49:56,134 --> 00:49:58,667
[After enjoying the provided tea & dessert]
enjoys the provided tea and dessert

1502
00:49:58,933 --> 00:50:01,703
[Shout "I am the prince!" to win]
you just have to shout "I am the prince!"

1503
00:50:01,704 --> 00:50:02,467
Oh, okay, okay.

1504
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:05,800
Wait…They're really
giving me hope until the end!

1505
00:50:06,107 --> 00:50:07,300
The staff keeps giving me hope!

1506
00:50:07,301 --> 00:50:08,600
That fabric is different from ours.

1507
00:50:08,601 --> 00:50:09,500
It's the same.

1508
00:50:09,501 --> 00:50:10,904
- Oh, you can do it like this.
- It's the same. It's the same.

1509
00:50:10,905 --> 00:50:12,266
[Sharing info like a generous gift]
You can flip it, too. It's the same thing.

1510
00:50:12,367 --> 00:50:13,834
[Got it!]
We just have to figure it out.

1511
00:50:13,834 --> 00:50:15,000
Should we do this seriously?

1512
00:50:15,167 --> 00:50:19,400
[Staff] Since SHINDONG was
about to go, you can do it first.

1513
00:50:21,267 --> 00:50:23,500
They've done it a lot,
so they must have some tricks up their sleeves.

1514
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:25,400
[Setting up carefully]
Isn't it better to put one on that side?

1515
00:50:25,401 --> 00:50:27,400
- Should we put it on this side?
- Yes.

1516
00:50:27,467 --> 00:50:29,300
How many bottles
have you done so far?

1517
00:50:29,400 --> 00:50:31,367
[Team SHINDONG's best record: DAWN 5 bottles]
We just did 5 bottles.

1518
00:50:31,368 --> 00:50:33,700
- Really? DAWN did?
- Yeah, he got 5 standing, but failed.

1519
00:50:34,033 --> 00:50:35,400
[SHINDONG’s second attempt]
Challenge accepted!

1520
00:50:35,401 --> 00:50:36,133
Challenge accepted!

1521
00:50:36,134 --> 00:50:37,633
[Habitual lying]
This is our 3rd lockout!

1522
00:50:37,700 --> 00:50:39,367
[Shaking]

1523
00:50:45,633 --> 00:50:46,700
[Success]
Wow!!!

1524
00:50:47,333 --> 00:50:48,467
[Succeeded
before Team LEETEUK could even try]

1525
00:50:48,468 --> 00:50:50,067
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

1526
00:50:50,400 --> 00:50:54,000
[Electrifying]

1527
00:50:54,533 --> 00:50:55,433
You guys planned that, right?

1528
00:50:55,600 --> 00:50:58,600
[Impeccable timing, like they staged it]
No, we didn't! We didn't plan it.

1529
00:50:58,967 --> 00:51:01,267
I was honestly
so disappointed in SHINDONG.

1530
00:51:01,333 --> 00:51:02,800
No, like this guy…!

1531
00:51:03,067 --> 00:51:05,700
If this is the first time
the prince and pauper are being chosen on this trip,

1532
00:51:05,701 --> 00:51:08,667
we should all
try it a few times each!

1533
00:51:08,767 --> 00:51:12,567
But he nailed it in one try
and killed the vibe.

1534
00:51:13,033 --> 00:51:14,800
This guy's been
on air since forever.

1535
00:51:14,801 --> 00:51:17,133
I expected
more from him than that.

1536
00:51:17,134 --> 00:51:19,433
LEETEUK doesn't really
understand how editing works.

1537
00:51:19,434 --> 00:51:22,100
If you watch the full show later,
it'll be really entertaining.

1538
00:51:22,101 --> 00:51:23,600
You'll be clutching your stomach,
laughing nonstop,

1539
00:51:23,601 --> 00:51:25,333
to the point
you'll surprise yourself.

1540
00:51:25,600 --> 00:51:27,900
While I was practicing,
I thought, "For this…"

1541
00:51:28,067 --> 00:51:29,510
"Speed is everything!"

1542
00:51:29,511 --> 00:51:30,333
And…

1543
00:51:30,633 --> 00:51:32,700
It's not an arm snap!
It's a wrist snap!

1544
00:51:32,701 --> 00:51:33,700
Swish!

1545
00:51:33,933 --> 00:51:35,800
I went for it, and it worked!

1546
00:51:35,933 --> 00:51:38,667
Success!!!!

1547
00:51:38,967 --> 00:51:40,900
When SHINDONG
just pulled it out quickly…

1548
00:51:41,033 --> 00:51:42,433
The bottles went back and forth.

1549
00:51:42,600 --> 00:51:44,067
I thought
I was on the Viking ride.

1550
00:51:44,068 --> 00:51:45,133
They went back and forth,

1551
00:51:45,134 --> 00:51:47,600
and when they finally stopped,
I also returned to the middle.

1552
00:51:48,800 --> 00:51:50,833
That moment
was seriously electrifying.

1553
00:51:51,512 --> 00:51:54,689
[Gives him the chills thinking about it]
SHINDONG, my heart literally skipped a beat.

1554
00:51:54,697 --> 00:51:55,952
I was really surprised too.

1555
00:51:56,133 --> 00:51:59,433
[Strategist SHINDONG completes the final challenge]
They were like wobbling!

1556
00:51:59,700 --> 00:52:00,689
We just need to do this quickly!

1557
00:52:00,690 --> 00:52:01,311
Yeah, do it!

1558
00:52:01,312 --> 00:52:02,167
We can just do it quickly!

1559
00:52:02,168 --> 00:52:03,333
JISUNG, this one's on you.

1560
00:52:03,334 --> 00:52:05,167
Wow, how do I even do this?

1561
00:52:06,133 --> 00:52:07,767
Come on,
that one's impossible.

1562
00:52:07,833 --> 00:52:08,800
One, two, three!

1563
00:52:08,801 --> 00:52:09,200
[Swoosh]

1564
00:52:09,600 --> 00:52:12,033
Oh, okay.
I got the vibe.

1565
00:52:12,034 --> 00:52:13,967
- It's not easy.
- It's hard, it's hard.

1566
00:52:14,200 --> 00:52:16,167
[Successful Team SHINDONG gets their tea & desserts]
Spread this on there.

1567
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:19,367
[The Full-Course Dining Mission: "The Pharaoh’s Table"]
[The Final Course]

1568
00:52:19,467 --> 00:52:21,667
[Staff] Team LEETEUK,
you can keep trying it.

1569
00:52:21,767 --> 00:52:23,100
But we have to
eat this quickly instead!

1570
00:52:23,300 --> 00:52:24,597
[Black tea & chocolate dates]
But hey, this is hot!

1571
00:52:24,598 --> 00:52:26,977
(Very hot)
How can you give us something hot in this weather?

1572
00:52:26,978 --> 00:52:27,719
JOHNNY's doing it!

1573
00:52:27,720 --> 00:52:29,733
[JOHNNY’s first attempt]
Let’s go!

1574
00:52:29,734 --> 00:52:30,633
[JOHNNY’s first fail]

1575
00:52:30,860 --> 00:52:33,093
[Busy / Chill]
But we have to enjoy it with ease.

1576
00:52:33,467 --> 00:52:35,967
[Starting with
a bite of the chocolate date]

1577
00:52:36,133 --> 00:52:38,167
I'm gonna watch them with ease!
Let's watch them!

1578
00:52:38,300 --> 00:52:40,200
[LEETEUK’s first try]
Challenge accepted!

1579
00:52:42,500 --> 00:52:43,166
Agh!!

1580
00:52:43,834 --> 00:52:44,800
Hey, eat faster.

1581
00:52:45,233 --> 00:52:47,333
Eat faster!

1582
00:52:48,900 --> 00:52:49,800
Ow, hot!

1583
00:52:49,801 --> 00:52:50,700
Hey, I think I can nail this.

1584
00:52:50,701 --> 00:52:53,233
[Way too hot to rush]
I think I can nail this.

1585
00:52:53,467 --> 00:52:55,967
[JISUNG’s second try]
Challenge accepted! One, two, three!

1586
00:52:55,968 --> 00:52:57,200
[JISUNG’s second fail]

1587
00:52:57,201 --> 00:52:59,700
Whew.

1588
00:53:00,233 --> 00:53:01,167
Ow, hot!

1589
00:53:01,533 --> 00:53:03,300
Hey, eat slowly!

1590
00:53:03,301 --> 00:53:04,733
You'll burn your tongue!

1591
00:53:05,100 --> 00:53:06,733
This is seriously hot.

1592
00:53:06,967 --> 00:53:09,100
[Sip]

1593
00:53:11,133 --> 00:53:12,067
Ack... hnng…

1594
00:53:12,267 --> 00:53:15,933
[The fail count keeps climbing]

1595
00:53:16,067 --> 00:53:17,500
I can relax a bit now.

1596
00:53:17,667 --> 00:53:18,696
I think I’m getting
the hang of this.

1597
00:53:18,697 --> 00:53:20,267
After two tries, I kinda get it.

1598
00:53:20,467 --> 00:53:21,190
- Is it this?
- Yeah.

1599
00:53:21,191 --> 00:53:24,033
[Starting to find their rhythm]
It's this, but in an instant…!

1600
00:53:24,067 --> 00:53:25,467
Team Pauper, you can do this!

1601
00:53:27,933 --> 00:53:29,600
[Received cheering that shattered their focus]
Wow, that's really triggering.

1602
00:53:29,601 --> 00:53:30,800
Let’s go, JISUNG!

1603
00:53:31,100 --> 00:53:32,367
[JISUNG’s third attempt]
Challenge accepted!

1604
00:53:32,633 --> 00:53:33,867
JISUNG’s pauper challenge!

1605
00:53:33,967 --> 00:53:34,800
Haha...

1606
00:53:34,801 --> 00:53:35,500
Two

1607
00:53:35,667 --> 00:53:36,800
[Fail]
Aw, man!

1608
00:53:36,967 --> 00:53:39,800
[Meanwhile,
SHINDONG clears the tea & the dessert]

1609
00:53:40,233 --> 00:53:42,233
[Fail]
Agh!

1610
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:44,733
[Fail]
So close.

1611
00:53:44,933 --> 00:53:45,633
[Wobble]

1612
00:53:45,634 --> 00:53:46,900
[Plop]
Wow.

1613
00:53:47,200 --> 00:53:47,833
Was that the wind…?

1614
00:53:47,834 --> 00:53:48,367
Okay…

1615
00:53:48,600 --> 00:53:51,467
[YOHAN clears his dessert]
Is something wrong on that side?

1616
00:53:51,700 --> 00:53:54,067
[A game full of romance]
Let’s just have fun and call it a day

1617
00:53:54,400 --> 00:53:56,667
You should still nail it once!

1618
00:53:56,833 --> 00:53:59,700
I have to show that I'm the big bro
at times like this! You saw it earlier, right?

1619
00:53:59,701 --> 00:54:00,600
You did it the best!

1620
00:54:00,800 --> 00:54:03,233
[The big bro who aims to be a solid leader]
Putting it near the edge!

1621
00:54:03,300 --> 00:54:05,900
[And the little bros
who watch with trust…]

1622
00:54:06,000 --> 00:54:08,133
Challenge accepted!

1623
00:54:10,267 --> 00:54:12,667
[Success]
Oh!

1624
00:54:12,833 --> 00:54:14,700
[This team's eldest seals the deal, too]
That's what I'm talking about.

1625
00:54:14,867 --> 00:54:15,967
Nice.

1626
00:54:16,333 --> 00:54:17,500
[Casually refilling the water]
Even refilling it.

1627
00:54:17,501 --> 00:54:18,400
Plenty of time for a refill.

1628
00:54:18,568 --> 00:54:20,333
I'll start over from the top, LEETEUK.

1629
00:54:20,500 --> 00:54:23,567
[Team LEETEUK gets their tea & dessert too]
Oh…

1630
00:54:23,733 --> 00:54:25,667
If you finish that quickly,
you could win!

1631
00:54:25,833 --> 00:54:27,267
[Chill]

1632
00:54:27,467 --> 00:54:30,000
Our concept is romance!

1633
00:54:30,133 --> 00:54:33,933
Because JOHNNY said
we're Team Romance.

1634
00:54:33,967 --> 00:54:36,033
Don’t lose our pace now.

1635
00:54:36,233 --> 00:54:38,033
[Keep it romantic till the end]
Keep it cool till the very last moment.

1636
00:54:38,133 --> 00:54:39,200
DAWN, let’s finish this.

1637
00:54:39,201 --> 00:54:40,300
Let's hurry and be princes.

1638
00:54:40,633 --> 00:54:41,800
I’m the pauper...

1639
00:54:42,067 --> 00:54:43,400
[Gulp]

1640
00:54:44,182 --> 00:54:44,967
I'm the prince.

1641
00:54:44,968 --> 00:54:45,900
One, two, three!

1642
00:54:46,200 --> 00:54:50,800
I’m the prince!

1643
00:54:51,600 --> 00:54:52,867
Nice…

1644
00:55:00,033 --> 00:55:05,133
[SHINDONG, DAWN, YOHAN
confirmed as the 1st princes]

1645
00:55:06,800 --> 00:55:07,867
Wow!

1646
00:55:07,868 --> 00:55:09,700
That was one long journey.

1647
00:55:09,701 --> 00:55:11,200
We had no idea we'd win.

1648
00:55:11,300 --> 00:55:14,900
I’m the prince!

1649
00:55:15,333 --> 00:55:16,933
But I really thought
we would lose.

1650
00:55:17,033 --> 00:55:18,013
We didn't pick a leader,

1651
00:55:18,014 --> 00:55:19,533
but I was
basically like the leader.

1652
00:55:20,033 --> 00:55:23,100
If they took my lead
and became paupers to sleep outside,

1653
00:55:23,101 --> 00:55:25,067
I think they would've blamed me.

1654
00:55:25,068 --> 00:55:26,367
Lucky for us,

1655
00:55:26,368 --> 00:55:27,933
we became princes!

1656
00:55:28,233 --> 00:55:29,500
Can I even say this?

1657
00:55:29,501 --> 00:55:32,133
I'm over the moon…?

1658
00:55:32,501 --> 00:55:34,300
Yeah, I think
that's the right word.

1659
00:55:34,733 --> 00:55:38,633
We were like,
hugging each other like crazy.

1660
00:55:38,767 --> 00:55:41,333
I was like, "What even is this..?"

1661
00:55:41,433 --> 00:55:44,767
[What even is this that it brought us together?]
I think we bonded hard then.

1662
00:55:45,700 --> 00:55:49,733
[Moving to their respective accommodations
based on their prince or pauper status]

1663
00:55:50,333 --> 00:55:51,200
We did it.

1664
00:55:52,100 --> 00:55:56,233
[The princes happily board the car]
We became princes.

1665
00:55:57,667 --> 00:56:01,233
[Caught the staff
chatting with the driver]

1666
00:56:03,900 --> 00:56:06,033
[Team Prince gains hotel intel]

1667
00:56:06,367 --> 00:56:08,900
(YOHAN instantly looks it up)
This is awesome.

1668
00:56:09,870 --> 00:56:11,867
- How did we actually win?
- Right?

1669
00:56:11,868 --> 00:56:12,600
Wow…

1670
00:56:13,167 --> 00:56:14,267
I pulled it,

1671
00:56:14,268 --> 00:56:16,333
[Looking back, the last mission was a nail-biter]
and it started shaking like crazy at first! Wow.

1672
00:56:16,334 --> 00:56:17,900
- Wow, seriously.
- You saw it earlier, right?

1673
00:56:17,901 --> 00:56:18,916
You thought they'd fall, right?

1674
00:56:18,917 --> 00:56:20,700
They would've fallen
if they had a little less water.

1675
00:56:21,767 --> 00:56:23,197
[Finished searching up the hotel]

1676
00:56:23,198 --> 00:56:26,733
One of Cairo’s
5-star hotels that's quite famous.

1677
00:56:26,734 --> 00:56:28,992
- Oh!
- Wow, it's gonna be amazing.

1678
00:56:28,993 --> 00:56:32,033
[A royal family villa that became a hotel!]
It was later renovated as a hotel.

1679
00:56:32,397 --> 00:56:36,433
[Prince's accommodation, Day 1]
There’s a lobby outside that feels like a real palace.

1680
00:56:38,567 --> 00:56:41,567
[Situated in front
of the Giza Plateau]

1681
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:47,567
[A 5-star hotel
with a view of the pyramids!]

1682
00:56:51,203 --> 00:56:55,167
[And the princes' room there]
Let's go and see what the princes' rooms are like!

1683
00:56:57,453 --> 00:57:02,204
[On the way to see it now]

1684
00:57:02,205 --> 00:57:04,067
Wow, I think
it's gonna be incredible.

1685
00:57:04,867 --> 00:57:06,100
[A grand hallway welcomes the princes]
It’s got serious vibes.

1686
00:57:06,101 --> 00:57:08,233
Wow, this is…

1687
00:57:08,626 --> 00:57:11,126
There’s definitely
a different vibe here.

1688
00:57:11,127 --> 00:57:13,260
- The hotel hallway is huge.
- Exactly, compared to everything so far.

1689
00:57:13,268 --> 00:57:15,000
[Totally blown away from the hallway]
The hallway is so huge.

1690
00:57:15,001 --> 00:57:17,000
Wow, this hallway
is seriously so wide.

1691
00:57:17,501 --> 00:57:20,767
You know, the fancier the hotel,
the fewer floors it actually has?

1692
00:57:21,600 --> 00:57:22,900
It’s long.

1693
00:57:22,901 --> 00:57:25,399
That’s why
the hallway’s super wide.

1694
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:27,267
I’ve never seen
such a wide hotel hallway before!

1695
00:57:28,093 --> 00:57:31,593
[The majestic hallway
raises expectations even more]

1696
00:57:32,200 --> 00:57:34,002
[Full of heart flutters]

1697
00:57:34,601 --> 00:57:36,102
Wow, I’m getting excited.

1698
00:57:36,111 --> 00:57:36,810
Hey, it's here.

1699
00:57:36,811 --> 00:57:38,994
[The princes each find their rooms]
My room's here.

1700
00:57:38,995 --> 00:57:40,905
This is my room.

1701
00:57:40,906 --> 00:57:42,400
Go find your rooms now.

1702
00:57:42,401 --> 00:57:43,091
Yes.

1703
00:57:43,533 --> 00:57:46,800
[The song that unites all generations kicks in]
Ppara-ppara-ppam!

1704
00:57:46,801 --> 00:57:48,933
- Ppara-ppara!
- Ppara-ppara!

1705
00:57:49,967 --> 00:57:53,490
[In awe from the first step in]
Wow!

1706
00:57:53,491 --> 00:57:55,000
Wow!

1707
00:57:55,500 --> 00:57:56,433
Wow!

1708
00:57:56,434 --> 00:57:59,078
[Befitting a royal villa]
Just amazing…!

1709
00:57:59,079 --> 00:58:00,200
Wow!

1710
00:58:01,633 --> 00:58:03,333
[An accommodation
with a classic vibe]

1711
00:58:04,533 --> 00:58:07,100
[A pyramid-view terrace included!]

1712
00:58:08,000 --> 00:58:11,400
[It's the breakfast spot
with an absolutely gorgeous view]

1713
00:58:12,384 --> 00:58:13,733
Oh!

1714
00:58:13,734 --> 00:58:17,100
[Officially checking out the room]
Yes, the hotel's the way to go!

1715
00:58:17,101 --> 00:58:18,800
Alright, let’s see
what we've got here.

1716
00:58:21,210 --> 00:58:21,917
What is this?

1717
00:58:22,712 --> 00:58:23,405
Wow…!

1718
00:58:24,867 --> 00:58:27,867
[The moment he spots the terrace]
Oh!

1719
00:58:28,433 --> 00:58:31,433
[Cheers explode]
Oh!

1720
00:58:35,733 --> 00:58:39,167
[The prince is loving this terrace]
Wow, this terrace is the best.

1721
00:58:40,600 --> 00:58:42,167
[A special performance
just for the prince’s arrival!]

1722
00:58:42,168 --> 00:58:45,000
[So exciting]

1723
00:58:45,001 --> 00:58:46,300
Wow.

1724
00:58:48,902 --> 00:58:49,800
First…

1725
00:58:49,801 --> 00:58:51,867
Let me just lie here for a second.

1726
00:58:52,810 --> 00:58:53,503
Ugh…

1727
00:58:54,267 --> 00:58:57,000
[Dives straight onto the bed]
AGH!

1728
00:58:57,001 --> 00:58:59,000
This is so nice.

1729
00:59:00,467 --> 00:59:03,267
[This is what being a prince is all about]
I could just fall asleep right now.

1730
00:59:03,809 --> 00:59:04,617
Oh, what's this?

1731
00:59:04,618 --> 00:59:05,903
[Meanwhile, DAWN and YOHAN…]

1732
00:59:05,904 --> 00:59:07,966
This place is so pleasant.

1733
00:59:09,600 --> 00:59:11,100
[Terrace spotted]
A terrace!

1734
00:59:11,101 --> 00:59:12,933
- Wow!
- There's a terrace! Wow!

1735
00:59:13,800 --> 00:59:16,700
There's a performance
going on over there right now!

1736
00:59:16,964 --> 00:59:18,001
It's this kind of vibe!

1737
00:59:18,002 --> 00:59:20,100
They're performing over there!

1738
00:59:20,101 --> 00:59:23,800
[Enjoying the terrace concert
in the middle of the night]

1739
00:59:24,512 --> 00:59:27,433
[All the princes fall for the terrace view]
The view was nice, and it was completely wide open.

1740
00:59:27,533 --> 00:59:29,888
"So, this is what
success really tastes like…"

1741
00:59:29,889 --> 00:59:32,033
That’s what I realized.

1742
00:59:32,034 --> 00:59:34,000
Coincidentally, there happened
to be a wedding going on over there!

1743
00:59:34,001 --> 00:59:36,214
[Prince SHINDONG loved it all, including the performance]
So, the lights were moving all over the place.

1744
00:59:36,214 --> 00:59:37,509
EDM was playing.

1745
00:59:37,509 --> 00:59:38,467
Wow!

1746
00:59:38,899 --> 00:59:40,489
I realized it today.

1747
00:59:40,490 --> 00:59:41,600
I am

1748
00:59:41,601 --> 00:59:45,633
[With a vow to be a prince again tomorrow]
determined to be a prince again tomorrow

1749
00:59:46,333 --> 00:59:50,000
[Time to hit the hay]

1750
00:59:50,533 --> 00:59:52,567
I wonder
what the paupers are up to.

1751
00:59:53,000 --> 00:59:55,233
Paupers, show yourselves!

1752
00:59:56,000 --> 00:59:57,767
[Team Pauper appears in low spirits]

1753
00:59:57,768 --> 00:59:59,700
[Gloomy]
[Mixed feelings]

1754
00:59:59,701 --> 01:00:03,933
[Even at Team Pauper's accommodation]
As you all loved earlier, the pauper accommodation

1755
01:00:03,934 --> 01:00:06,033
[There is romance…?]
is a place full of romance.

1756
01:00:07,126 --> 01:00:08,704
It's full of romance?

1757
01:00:08,705 --> 01:00:09,659
Full of romance.

1758
01:00:10,200 --> 01:00:11,000
So, in a way

1759
01:00:11,001 --> 01:00:12,633
[Add romance]
In a way, it could be romantic, right?

1760
01:00:12,634 --> 01:00:14,799
[To romance]
Let’s just choose romance.

1761
01:00:14,800 --> 01:00:16,300
[And to more romance]
We agreed to go for romance.

1762
01:00:16,667 --> 01:00:17,667
[JOHNNY was on Team Romance all day]
We chased after romance!

1763
01:00:17,668 --> 01:00:19,300
We're chasing after romance.

1764
01:00:19,301 --> 01:00:20,400
Nice, nice.

1765
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:21,800
I think…

1766
01:00:21,801 --> 01:00:24,067
[No more romance]
we don't need to be romantic now.

1767
01:00:24,723 --> 01:00:25,633
We chased after romance,

1768
01:00:25,634 --> 01:00:28,567
[Giving up on romance after becoming a pauper]
and found hardship.

1769
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,933
[According to JOHNNY, the ultimate romantic...]
My basic aesthetic is chasing after romance!

1770
01:00:31,400 --> 01:00:35,700
If a trip is too easy,
it won't be memorable.

1771
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:41,233
[So I’m choosing the hard life]
It's like, I'm searching for hardship.

1772
01:00:42,267 --> 01:00:44,233
(Why did I do that...)

1773
01:00:45,500 --> 01:00:50,367
[JISUNG, let's toss romance aside]

1774
01:00:50,767 --> 01:00:52,633
[Already given up]
Let's just go and sleep.

1775
01:00:53,533 --> 01:00:55,397
[A dark path ahead, just like how they feel...]
The road ahead is pitch black.

1776
01:00:55,398 --> 01:00:57,467
It’s so dark,
just like my feelings

1777
01:00:58,433 --> 01:01:01,567
[A brutal off-road trail appears]
The boulders up ahead are insane!

1778
01:01:01,900 --> 01:01:03,000
I hate this so much.

1779
01:01:04,300 --> 01:01:05,503
I really hate this.

1780
01:01:05,504 --> 01:01:06,533
Oh…!

1781
01:01:07,633 --> 01:01:11,633
[A special service for Team Pauper]
I'm sorry, but I'm not gonna be a pauper!

1782
01:01:12,667 --> 01:01:15,067
[Off-road romance]
Please just send me home already.

1783
01:01:15,068 --> 01:01:17,000
That was legendary just now.

1784
01:01:17,496 --> 01:01:18,685
Wow, that was seriously legendary.

1785
01:01:18,685 --> 01:01:21,067
[Finally, Team Pauper arrives somewhere]
How far are we going in?

1786
01:01:22,267 --> 01:01:24,495
[First getting out into the darkness]

1787
01:01:24,496 --> 01:01:25,467
Wow…

1788
01:01:25,468 --> 01:01:26,100
Wow…!

1789
01:01:26,867 --> 01:01:28,767
I can see the stars!

1790
01:01:28,800 --> 01:01:30,600
[They said no more romance,
but the younger paupers keep searching for it]

1791
01:01:30,601 --> 01:01:32,367
You can see them.

1792
01:01:32,368 --> 01:01:33,667
I can see one.

1793
01:01:33,668 --> 01:01:35,000
It must be a satellite.

1794
01:01:35,298 --> 01:01:37,725
If we turn off the lights,
we could probably see them better.

1795
01:01:37,726 --> 01:01:39,633
[Cairo is a famous spot for stars]

1796
01:01:39,887 --> 01:01:42,300
[Forget adventure, the older pauper is just tired]
It’s 1:20 a.m. right now.

1797
01:01:42,301 --> 01:01:45,402
We’ve been awake
for almost 40 hours straight,

1798
01:01:45,403 --> 01:01:47,100
and we have to
be up again in 4 hours.

1799
01:01:47,101 --> 01:01:49,696
But can the camera
even capture this right now?

1800
01:01:50,000 --> 01:01:52,567
Just how far…

1801
01:01:52,568 --> 01:01:53,867
Can people see where we are?

1802
01:01:54,233 --> 01:01:56,833
[This pitch-dark place is actually]

1803
01:01:57,667 --> 01:02:00,000
[A chill camping spot with all the vibes]

1804
01:02:00,267 --> 01:02:01,278
[Wadi Degla Protectorate]

1805
01:02:01,291 --> 01:02:03,212
[This was filmed safely with
prior permission from the authorities]

1806
01:02:06,533 --> 01:02:11,033
[The first pauper accommodation]
The first "ALL or NOTHING" pauper accommodation is this way.

1807
01:02:11,200 --> 01:02:11,967
Hold up.

1808
01:02:11,968 --> 01:02:12,999
[The pauper vibe is stronger than imagined]
Oh, please, no…

1809
01:02:13,000 --> 01:02:15,005
- This is the real pauper life
- Oh, wait.

1810
01:02:15,006 --> 01:02:17,367
Wow, this is legit pauper status.

1811
01:02:18,433 --> 01:02:20,967
Wow, I'm really a pauper…

1812
01:02:20,968 --> 01:02:22,467
This is all real.

1813
01:02:22,468 --> 01:02:24,734
[Who am I? Where am I?]
Wow. Why am I here, plus…

1814
01:02:24,735 --> 01:02:25,834
I realized that

1815
01:02:25,834 --> 01:02:27,201
[Baby JISUNG thrown]
I've been really spoiled,

1816
01:02:27,201 --> 01:02:28,485
[into this brutal variety show world]
and I've been a pretty happy guy

1817
01:02:28,486 --> 01:02:30,133
all this time.

1818
01:02:30,500 --> 01:02:31,833
Honestly, I was kinda stunned.

1819
01:02:31,834 --> 01:02:33,467
I didn’t expect it
to be this intense.

1820
01:02:33,967 --> 01:02:37,667
[Left stranded in a barren desert...]
I had no clue they’d just dump us here.

1821
01:02:38,867 --> 01:02:41,267
That wasn't an accommodation!

1822
01:02:41,597 --> 01:02:43,633
[Pure shock]
I was so shook. For real.

1823
01:02:43,634 --> 01:02:46,000
Shouldn’t there be
at least a ceiling or something?

1824
01:02:46,092 --> 01:02:47,198
Oh, LEETEUK.

1825
01:02:47,199 --> 01:02:48,900
[JOHNNY looks excited, considering he was left behind]
If you ask me, this is that.

1826
01:02:48,901 --> 01:02:49,809
We set it?

1827
01:02:49,810 --> 01:02:51,266
This is a tent.

1828
01:02:51,396 --> 01:02:52,300
It's a tent?

1829
01:02:52,490 --> 01:02:53,633
- LEETEUK.
- Yeah.

1830
01:02:53,634 --> 01:02:56,633
[Big smile]
Seriously, just once, just once!

1831
01:02:56,634 --> 01:02:57,867
Stop spewing nonsense.

1832
01:02:57,868 --> 01:02:58,886
Just open it once.

1833
01:02:58,887 --> 01:02:59,873
- Open what?
- Your heart.

1834
01:02:59,874 --> 01:03:01,134
[JOHNNY / LEETEUK]
[Romantic Team Pauper's spear and shield]

1835
01:03:01,134 --> 01:03:01,994
It is pretty cool.

1836
01:03:01,995 --> 01:03:03,267
What's cool?

1837
01:03:03,495 --> 01:03:05,390
[The unbreakable romantic shield]
It's so dark, you can't even see anything.

1838
01:03:05,391 --> 01:03:07,633
Isn't it cool because it's dark?

1839
01:03:08,967 --> 01:03:11,600
[The pauper leader assesses the situation]
What's this?

1840
01:03:12,077 --> 01:03:14,933
[Checking supplies]
They only gave us three bottles of water.

1841
01:03:15,100 --> 01:03:16,733
Three measly bottles of water?!

1842
01:03:20,492 --> 01:03:21,600
It’s a humidifying mask.

1843
01:03:21,867 --> 01:03:24,967
[The survival kit includes humidifying masks and bread]
A humidifying mask…

1844
01:03:25,389 --> 01:03:26,000
From what I can tell,

1845
01:03:26,001 --> 01:03:26,982
[Today's home: Tent found]
it's a tent.

1846
01:03:26,983 --> 01:03:27,802
Open it up.

1847
01:03:27,803 --> 01:03:28,677
Yeah, that must be it.

1848
01:03:28,678 --> 01:03:29,417
Go ahead and open it.

1849
01:03:31,033 --> 01:03:33,300
LEETEUK, have you ever
set up a tent before?

1850
01:03:33,704 --> 01:03:36,099
[Can only trust LEETEUK, who's served in the army]
It’s been ages since I set up a tent.

1851
01:03:36,100 --> 01:03:38,266
First, you have to untie this.

1852
01:03:38,733 --> 01:03:42,333
[Even though he has mixed feelings…]
Hah…

1853
01:03:42,334 --> 01:03:44,267
[When his younger bros seek him out]
Wait, wait, what's this?

1854
01:03:44,268 --> 01:03:45,200
Isn't this

1855
01:03:45,208 --> 01:03:47,907
[He transforms into a grumbling problem-solver]
one of those pop-up tents?

1856
01:03:48,074 --> 01:03:49,516
Don't you just spread it open?

1857
01:03:49,890 --> 01:03:50,867
Wow, that's a relief!

1858
01:03:50,868 --> 01:03:52,298
[LEETEUK naturally takes charge]
Wow.

1859
01:03:52,299 --> 01:03:53,800
That’s a relief.

1860
01:03:54,500 --> 01:03:55,900
[Immediately figured out the tent]
Oh, this is that. It just sets up.

1861
01:03:55,901 --> 01:03:57,367
Wow, thank goodness, for real.

1862
01:03:57,933 --> 01:03:59,600
[The grumbling pauper suddenly takes the lead]
Hey, hey, this one, over here on the side.

1863
01:03:59,601 --> 01:04:01,200
Oh, what?
This is super convenient!

1864
01:04:01,667 --> 01:04:04,200
Isn't this only for one person?

1865
01:04:04,767 --> 01:04:07,467
[Complaints bubble up again]
This isn't the Han River or anything!

1866
01:04:07,993 --> 01:04:11,500
[But his younger bros seem super hyped]
Hey, but it’s pretty spacious!

1867
01:04:11,501 --> 01:04:13,300
No, like, more than expected.

1868
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:15,167
Do you guys…

1869
01:04:15,168 --> 01:04:15,867
find this fun?

1870
01:04:17,567 --> 01:04:19,183
[Yeah, it’s fun]
It is kind of fun.

1871
01:04:19,184 --> 01:04:20,667
It's fun? Sigh…!

1872
01:04:21,433 --> 01:04:23,333
I was seriously so mad,

1873
01:04:23,334 --> 01:04:26,811
but they kept saying,
"LEETEUK, this is so great!"

1874
01:04:26,812 --> 01:04:29,299
JOHNNY's like,
"LEETEUK, this is so romantic."

1875
01:04:29,867 --> 01:04:31,023
[The oldest pauper
gets more and more conflicted]

1876
01:04:31,024 --> 01:04:32,617
- It is kind of fun.
- Yeah, it's fun.

1877
01:04:32,618 --> 01:04:34,133
It's fun? Sigh…!

1878
01:04:34,134 --> 01:04:34,767
But wait a sec,

1879
01:04:34,768 --> 01:04:36,767
we're right on top of a boulder.

1880
01:04:37,033 --> 01:04:38,667
Let’s find somewhere flat!

1881
01:04:39,267 --> 01:04:40,100
[LEETEUK trait]

1882
01:04:40,101 --> 01:04:42,033
[Complains, but works the hardest]
Right here.

1883
01:04:43,433 --> 01:04:44,900
[Thanks to the grumbling pauper's efforts,
the pauper accommodation is finally complete]

1884
01:04:44,901 --> 01:04:47,367
JISUNG, do you like it?

1885
01:04:48,092 --> 01:04:49,105
[Next quest]
I have a feeling that

1886
01:04:49,106 --> 01:04:50,833
[Laying out the mat inside the tent]
we can't spread this out completely.

1887
01:04:50,834 --> 01:04:52,698
[For some reason]
We gotta fold it up about this much

1888
01:04:52,699 --> 01:04:54,433
[The grumbling pauper is holding it]
to use it.

1889
01:04:55,067 --> 01:04:56,018
LEETEUK, please do it.

1890
01:04:56,019 --> 01:04:57,402
Move aside.

1891
01:04:57,767 --> 01:04:59,500
[So fed up]
Ugh!!!

1892
01:04:59,690 --> 01:05:01,484
[ROMANTIC BABOZ]
Hey, you were so eager to do this earlier,

1893
01:05:01,485 --> 01:05:03,067
[who don't know how to do anything]
but now that we're doing it…

1894
01:05:03,395 --> 01:05:06,001
[LEETEUK eventually steps in]
But because you are good at this…

1895
01:05:06,002 --> 01:05:07,400
No, it's not
that I'm good at this.

1896
01:05:08,691 --> 01:05:11,095
[The grumbling pauper still works hard]
We can't do anything about this.

1897
01:05:11,095 --> 01:05:13,421
- It just needs to overlap.
- Yeah, let's spread it out,

1898
01:05:13,422 --> 01:05:14,692
and just…

1899
01:05:15,387 --> 01:05:17,484
[Leads by example + Gives clear orders = Great leader]
Remember those big rocks from before?

1900
01:05:17,485 --> 01:05:19,306
Put them on the inside, like this.

1901
01:05:19,307 --> 01:05:20,800
Hand me a rock.

1902
01:05:20,801 --> 01:05:23,711
[Mentally checked out]
Ugh!!

1903
01:05:23,712 --> 01:05:24,632
I just wanna go home!!

1904
01:05:24,633 --> 01:05:26,397
[But he's physically working hard]
Hand me a rock.

1905
01:05:26,405 --> 01:05:27,833
Ugh!!!

1906
01:05:29,667 --> 01:05:31,933
[He's definitely a good leader]
Oh, but LEETEUK really did it well for us.

1907
01:05:33,400 --> 01:05:34,491
[I invite you to my pauper tent]
Come in.

1908
01:05:34,492 --> 01:05:37,290
But aren't deserts
supposed to get cold at night?

1909
01:05:38,167 --> 01:05:41,567
[Zen mode activated]
You'll get cold as you sleep.

1910
01:05:42,110 --> 01:05:43,097
JISUNG, come inside.

1911
01:05:45,667 --> 01:05:47,800
I really don't think
this place is right…What do you think?

1912
01:05:48,526 --> 01:05:51,126
- It's alright, though.
- It's not so bad.

1913
01:05:51,403 --> 01:05:52,300
It's not bad.

1914
01:05:52,301 --> 01:05:53,800
It's bad!!!

1915
01:05:53,967 --> 01:05:57,667
If we had a fire and some ramyeon,
it'd be perfect.

1916
01:05:57,668 --> 01:05:59,700
[What do you mean? We have neither]
We don't have a fire or ramyeon.

1917
01:05:59,701 --> 01:06:00,867
- That's why I'm bummed.
- No, so like…

1918
01:06:00,868 --> 01:06:01,933
Don't think about the "What ifs"!

1919
01:06:01,934 --> 01:06:05,067
[The pauper leader is sharp at reading the situation]
Take a moment and look at the situation we're in!

1920
01:06:06,833 --> 01:06:08,533
If this place isn't so bad,

1921
01:06:08,534 --> 01:06:10,033
then are you
gonna keep being paupers?

1922
01:06:10,567 --> 01:06:12,767
Think about Team Prince!

1923
01:06:12,768 --> 01:06:14,400
Right now, they're comfortably

1924
01:06:14,401 --> 01:06:15,800
[The leader tries]
sleeping on king-sized beds.

1925
01:06:15,801 --> 01:06:18,998
[to motivate the team members]
They have their own rooms and can have hot showers.

1926
01:06:18,999 --> 01:06:21,800
They probably started sleeping, like 1-2 hours ago.

1927
01:06:23,033 --> 01:06:24,600
- Here are your final supplies.
- Oh? What's this?

1928
01:06:24,601 --> 01:06:25,800
[Bedding is provided for the paupers]
This is a sleeping bag.

1929
01:06:26,100 --> 01:06:27,499
[Romantic JOHNNY is happy even with a sleeping bag]
Oh!

1930
01:06:27,500 --> 01:06:28,733
How do we use this?

1931
01:06:29,600 --> 01:06:31,200
It gets hot in here.

1932
01:06:32,090 --> 01:06:34,979
[The grumpy pauper
wants a room of his own]

1933
01:06:34,988 --> 01:06:37,067
Ugh…

1934
01:06:37,467 --> 01:06:39,994
[Successfully moved out]
JOHNNY.

1935
01:06:39,995 --> 01:06:40,902
JOHNNY.

1936
01:06:41,484 --> 01:06:42,597
But LEETEUK.

1937
01:06:42,598 --> 01:06:43,091
Yeah?

1938
01:06:43,092 --> 01:06:46,500
[JOHNNY is still a positive romantic]
Your body is gonna feel so refreshed.

1939
01:06:46,691 --> 01:06:48,275
[This isn't just a foot reflexology]
It's like those acupressure slippers,

1940
01:06:48,276 --> 01:06:50,500
[It’s a full-body reflexology!]
but actually, acupressure for the body!

1941
01:06:50,501 --> 01:06:51,233
Acupressure for the body.

1942
01:06:52,233 --> 01:06:54,700
This is not the time to be laughing.

1943
01:06:55,005 --> 01:06:57,406
[With his back to his team members]
We have to win no matter what tomorrow

1944
01:06:57,407 --> 01:06:59,367
[the leader lays down his vision]
and become princes!

1945
01:06:59,368 --> 01:07:00,100
You know?

1946
01:07:00,101 --> 01:07:02,667
But I don't think
we'll be on the same team.

1947
01:07:03,095 --> 01:07:04,990
[Suddenly JOHNNY goes into savage mode]
JOHNNY, were you always this cold?

1948
01:07:04,991 --> 01:07:07,000
Yes.

1949
01:07:07,001 --> 01:07:08,509
[LEETEUK gets
abandoned by the Romantics]

1950
01:07:08,510 --> 01:07:10,667
Ugh! I'm so annoyed!

1951
01:07:11,233 --> 01:07:14,133
I need to ditch these guys.

1952
01:07:14,134 --> 01:07:15,900
I need to survive on my own.

1953
01:07:15,901 --> 01:07:17,967
I shouldn't do team battles.

1954
01:07:18,303 --> 01:07:19,100
JISUNG and JOHNNY…

1955
01:07:19,101 --> 01:07:20,696
[Team Pauper is falling apart?!?]
I have to ditch them.

1956
01:07:20,697 --> 01:07:22,000
That thought crossed my mind.

1957
01:07:22,305 --> 01:07:23,033
You're so cold.

1958
01:07:23,034 --> 01:07:24,633
I’m feeling so lonely right now.

1959
01:07:25,167 --> 01:07:27,600
Come inside, LEETEUK.

1960
01:07:27,601 --> 01:07:28,867
I should just
use this as a pillow.

1961
01:07:28,868 --> 01:07:31,200
[Before LEETEUK's return]
Oh, this isn’t so bad.

1962
01:07:31,201 --> 01:07:32,267
[The pauper siblings tidy things up]
I’ll just use it as a pillow.

1963
01:07:38,033 --> 01:07:42,100
[The grumpy pauper
eventually heads back inside]

1964
01:07:42,900 --> 01:07:45,933
[Always keeps his bedding neat]

1965
01:07:47,800 --> 01:07:49,194
[ROMANTIC BABOZ
are still quite satisfied]

1966
01:07:49,195 --> 01:07:50,286
Wow, LEETEUK.

1967
01:07:50,287 --> 01:07:51,367
But LEETEUK,
this is really nice!

1968
01:07:52,000 --> 01:07:53,067
[I don't like it!!!!]
Ugh!!!

1969
01:07:54,409 --> 01:07:58,033
[Time for the paupers to sleep]
Paupers, get some good sleep tonight.

1970
01:07:58,034 --> 01:07:59,408
Are you really
leaving us like this?

1971
01:07:59,409 --> 01:08:00,800
We're sleeping
right next to you, too.

1972
01:08:01,284 --> 01:08:05,933
But you calling
a pauper "a pauper"…

1973
01:08:05,934 --> 01:08:08,533
As a pauper,
it's really offensive!

1974
01:08:08,780 --> 01:08:10,700
- Now that I think about it, yeah…
- It makes you angry, right?

1975
01:08:10,701 --> 01:08:12,600
- That is really annoying.
- Hey, JOHNNY. You have to remember that!

1976
01:08:12,601 --> 01:08:15,700
[Only mad now after someone called him a pauper]
We need to leave this pauper life behind.

1977
01:08:16,192 --> 01:08:19,392
[The paupers are so different from the princes]
Honestly, I’ve just given up.

1978
01:08:19,799 --> 01:08:21,085
I'll see you in the morning.

1979
01:08:21,300 --> 01:08:24,467
[Trying to turn off the tent light...]
How do I turn this off?

1980
01:08:25,501 --> 01:08:26,308
UGH!

1981
01:08:26,999 --> 01:08:29,107
[The paupers can't even turn off the light]
There's nothing Team Pauper can do…

1982
01:08:29,108 --> 01:08:31,200
Can't even turn off the light.

1983
01:08:31,767 --> 01:08:33,600
[While fiddling with the light]

1984
01:08:33,601 --> 01:08:34,899
[A club opens]

1985
01:08:34,900 --> 01:08:36,734
- This is a club.
- Wow, it's a club!

1986
01:08:36,891 --> 01:08:37,833
Whoo!

1987
01:08:37,834 --> 01:08:39,693
[A special desert club
created just for the romantic Team Pauper]

1988
01:08:39,700 --> 01:08:41,472
So it has this feature too.

1989
01:08:41,714 --> 01:08:42,767
- Is it okay?
- No.

1990
01:08:42,768 --> 01:08:44,133
[It's really bedtime now]

1991
01:08:44,134 --> 01:08:45,497
Oh, there we go.

1992
01:08:45,498 --> 01:08:46,397
Ugh.

1993
01:08:47,933 --> 01:08:48,698
Let's be princes tomorrow.

1994
01:08:48,699 --> 01:08:50,399
[Falling asleep,
determined to be a prince tomorrow]

1995
01:08:50,400 --> 01:08:51,685
I'm gonna do it.

1996
01:08:51,686 --> 01:08:52,598
I'm gonna do it.

1997
01:08:52,599 --> 01:08:53,533
Me too.

1998
01:08:54,608 --> 01:08:55,708
That feeling starts to set in.

1999
01:08:56,467 --> 01:08:59,767
"I'm really not
gonna be a pauper."

2000
01:08:59,768 --> 01:09:03,667
I promised myself
that I would definitely be a prince.

2001
01:09:04,433 --> 01:09:08,300
No matter what happens tomorrow,
I’m gonna be a prince

2002
01:09:09,033 --> 01:09:10,810
[And so, everyone]
I became so determined that I thought,

2003
01:09:10,811 --> 01:09:13,467
[dreams of moving up]
"Whether I look good or bad on camera,"

2004
01:09:13,468 --> 01:09:14,590
"I'm gonna be a prince."

2005
01:09:15,390 --> 01:09:16,200
Goodnight, everyone.

2006
01:09:16,201 --> 01:09:17,896
[Will they really
become princes tomorrow…?]

2007
01:09:17,897 --> 01:09:18,798
Good night.

2008
01:09:18,799 --> 01:09:20,400
Sleep well.

2009
01:09:20,633 --> 01:09:23,133
[Everything changes for next week]
[Egypt Trip, Day 2]

2010
01:09:23,517 --> 01:09:24,717
Let's go to the next stop.

2011
01:09:24,718 --> 01:09:27,333
["ALL or NOTHING" heads to a new city]
Let’s go!

2012
01:09:28,900 --> 01:09:30,010
[LUXOR]
Luxor.

2013
01:09:30,011 --> 01:09:30,816
This is so cool.

2014
01:09:30,817 --> 01:09:32,333
How is this
still standing after all this time?

2015
01:09:32,334 --> 01:09:34,232
[The world’s largest outdoor museum]
Whoa, this is pretty cool.

2016
01:09:34,233 --> 01:09:35,817
[Where the dead and living meet]
The prime resting place of kings.

2017
01:09:35,818 --> 01:09:36,667
Wow, look at this!

2018
01:09:37,000 --> 01:09:39,567
[Waiting for them there is...]
Oh, there’s a pool!

2019
01:09:39,900 --> 01:09:42,293
[The highlight of the Luxor trip]
Wow, Luxor!

2020
01:09:42,294 --> 01:09:43,800
The game's over.

2021
01:09:43,801 --> 01:09:45,309
This is serious luxury.

2022
01:09:45,310 --> 01:09:46,700
[Luxury cruise]
Wow, this is insane.

2023
01:09:47,373 --> 01:09:48,803
[Excitement level 100%]
Wow!

2024
01:09:48,804 --> 01:09:49,967
- This is nuts!
- So crazy!

2025
01:09:50,433 --> 01:09:52,100
[If you’re a pauper, you can't get on board]
Isn’t this too good to be true?

2026
01:09:52,101 --> 01:09:54,067
Wow, this place is amazing.

2027
01:09:54,400 --> 01:09:55,700
Let’s just travel
without battling.

2028
01:09:55,701 --> 01:09:58,167
Let's just all sleep together
without doing any missions!

2029
01:09:58,267 --> 01:10:00,167
[Nope, go back]

2030
01:10:00,433 --> 01:10:01,902
[To board]
The luggage is here! The luggage is here!

2031
01:10:01,903 --> 01:10:03,033
[You gotta take your luggage]
Wait, what is this?

2032
01:10:03,034 --> 01:10:04,102
[If you fail to save your luggage]
I haven't properly

2033
01:10:04,103 --> 01:10:05,467
unpacked my bags yet.

2034
01:10:05,468 --> 01:10:06,300
[Chosen as Today's Pauper]
Super poor!

2035
01:10:06,301 --> 01:10:07,533
Ugh, I hate this so much!

2036
01:10:07,534 --> 01:10:08,900
[To save your luggage]
This is going too far!

2037
01:10:08,901 --> 01:10:10,233
Way too far!

2038
01:10:10,234 --> 01:10:11,000
LEETEUK!

2039
01:10:11,001 --> 01:10:12,933
[Fight with everything you’ve got]
How are you supposed to run fast like this?

2040
01:10:13,267 --> 01:10:14,611
[Activate your brainpower!]
Wait, I know this one! Ugh!

2041
01:10:14,612 --> 01:10:16,433
Hold on, my memory is…!

2042
01:10:16,434 --> 01:10:17,300
[Their endlessly]
Ack!!

2043
01:10:17,301 --> 01:10:18,033
[Changing]
Woo-hoo!

2044
01:10:18,034 --> 01:10:18,800
[Fate]
Oh, this one…

2045
01:10:18,801 --> 01:10:19,767
Ack!

2046
01:10:19,768 --> 01:10:20,667
Wow!

2047
01:10:20,668 --> 01:10:21,900
Whoo!

2048
01:10:22,167 --> 01:11:37,272
[So, who’ll make it
onto the cruise as princes...?]
